namedrockunit:HISL
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use CIGSS] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for all components of the Caledonian Supersuite (CIGSS) that occur within the Northern Highlands and Grampian Highlands regions and formed broadly in association with the Scandian Event. This is the younger (Silurian) of the two main tectonothermal events of the Caledonian Orogeny in Scotland. \r
\r
Term not currently used by BGS."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/S> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 4.431e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/S> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DL> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.943e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> ;
    skos:definition "Obsolete name. Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Silurian Period - to - Early Devonian Epoch (Devonian Period) (443.1-394.3 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "HISL"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Scottish Highlands Silurian Suite [Obsolete: use CIGSS]"@en ;
