namedrockunit:NWHAG
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/DMTN"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete] \r
\r
A suite of glacial, glaciofluvial and glaciolacustrine deposits that contain clasts derived predominantly from Lewisian, Torridonian, Cambrian, Caledonian igneous and Moine psammitic rocks of the northern Highlands. Including sandy diamictons (till), sand, gravel, silt and clay. Deposited by ice that radiated outwards from an ice divide positioned inland of the western seaboard of the Northern Highlands. \r
\r
Provisional term listed in McMillan et al. (2005) not required in the present framework."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Sharp, unconformable contact with bedrock."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QC> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 8.6e-01 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/UG> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "To 5m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Unconformable contact with units of the Northwest Highlands Glacigenic Subgroup, or Flandrian deposits, predominantly peat."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QO> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.26e-01 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> ;
    skos:definition "Obsolete name. Diamicton and gravel with subsidiary clay, sand and silt. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Cromerian Stage - to - Wolstonian Stage (Quaternary Period) (.86-.126 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "NWHAG"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Northwest Highlands (Albion) Glacigenic Subgroup [Obsolete]"@en ;
.

