namedrockunit:AFTL
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Stiff, calcareous, grey, silty clay with well dispersed small pebbles, shells, foraminiferids, ostracods and inclusions of diamicton, sand and gravel. The clay is generally massive although locally laminated with concentrations of dark minerals and/or organic material. The lenses of diamicton, sand and gravel are sparse and disrupted in deformation zones within a metre or so of the upper boundary.\r
The foraminiferal and dinoflagellate cyst associations present in the clay both indicate a cold but not fully glacial estuarine environment.Two samples of benthonic foramiferids from near the top of the sequence have yielded a Conventional Radiocarbon Age of 41002 +/- 803 years BP.The calculated Calendar age is 45,605+/-731 years BP (a minimum a Mid Devensian age).\r
The deposit is very likely to have been ice-rafted from an original position nearer to the coast to the west or from the Firth of Clyde."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Not observed, probably unconformable directly on bedrock, but possibly a gradational glacitectonic contact with underlying till."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.16e-01 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription ">5m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Either a sharp, concavo-convex to planar boundary with overlying reddish brown sandy, silty, clay with scattered cobbles (Auchenwinsey Till Member of the Wilderness Till Formation), or a gradational, glacitectonic boundary involving intercalation and intermixing with the overlying till."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.18e-02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:COAS ;
    skos:definition "Clay with subsidiary silt and trace gravel. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devensian Stage (Quaternary Period) (.116-.0118 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "AFTL"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Afton Lodge Clay Formation"@en ;
.

