        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/TUF"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Westerly derived pale yellow to buff, quartz-rich sandstones and pebbly sandstones with subordinate red mudstones and conglomerates, and thin air-fall dust and crystal-lithic tuffs. Hillier and Williams (2004) provided a recent description."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary of the formation is placed at the base of the pale quartz-rich sandstones, where they overlie red mudstones of the Red Cliff Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SU> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 4.267e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 95 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary is placed at the top of metre-thick, massive coarse-grained mud-matrix quartz-rich sandstones of the Albion Sands Formation, where they are succeeded conformably by red mudstones of the overlying Moor Cliffs (formerly Sandy Haven) Formation exposed at the base of Gateholm Stack [SM 773 075]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SO> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.19e+02 ;
