    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use CIGSS] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for major intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite (HIO) that occur in the Alford district and consist of dioritic to granitic rock. They are lithologically associated (diorite, quartz-diorite, tonalite, granodiorite and granite), and lithologically distinct from other intrusions of the Scottish Highlands Ordovician Suite. \r
\r
Term not currently used by BGS."""@en ;
