    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A lower unit, exposed only in the south-west, consists of 15 m of basaltic tuff overlain by a 6 m thick plagioclase-microphyric basalt to hawaiite lava (Jedburgh type). The overlying sequence consists of several flows of plagioclase-macrophyric basalt to hawaiite (Markle type) and two flows of mugearite."@en ;
