    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Locally brecciated andesite lavas, with thin intercalations of lapilli-tuff and volcaniclastic sandstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at the base of the autobrecciated andesite overlying a few metres of sandstone of the Esk Pike Sandstone Formation. In some poorly exposed areas it may overlie silicic lapilli-tuff of the Lincomb Tarns Tuff Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/O4> ;
