    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Top Beeston Coal is a bituminous coal of high economic importance that was mined principally in the area southeast of Leeds. It splits westwards, the upper part forming the Churwell Thin Coal, the lower portion forming the top of the Churwell Thick."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CA> ;
