        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Silty clay, calcareous, laminated, very stiff, dark brown (Munsell Soil), with sparse dropstone pebbles and cold marine microflora. Laminae are stacked within graded, rhythmic units."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Gradational, conformable contact with underlying laminated silt and clay of the Carleton Silt Formation."@en ;
