        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Chenier deposits comprise sand occupying a long, low, narrow, wooded beach ridge or hummock which forms roughly parallel to a prograding shoreline, resting on peat or clay. Width varies from 40 to 400 m and length can be several tens of kilometres. \r
\r
Sand and gravel; inter-chenier deposits are typically more clay- and silt-rich."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.58e+00 ;
