        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Comprises banded mudstones and siltstones. Very minor sandstones. Banding is characteristically wide - 10-30cm +, is common. May reach 60cm. Turbiditic mudstones overlain by oxic or anoxic hemipelagite intervals. Graptolitic units may be present."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken to be at the base of a laterally traceable anoxic mudstone (graptolitic) horizon (7878 0050)."@en ;
