    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Generally up to 1 to 2m, 6m locally; 4m at the type locality [SO 235 127]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top is placed at the incoming of well-bedded, thinly bedded, cyclic limestones (the Chelternham Limestone Member), where the basal bed of limestone sharply overlies the topmost green clay or rubbly limestone of the Clydach Halt Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.43e+02 ;
