    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Flint-rich sand and gravel containing numerous clasts of vein quartz and quartzite with far-travelled erratics of dolerite, schist, greywacke, Old Red Sandstone, granodiorite and porphyry. They possess a wide range of sedimentary structures including horizontal and planar cross-bedding and ripple drift cross-lamination and were deposited as proximal glaciofluvial deposits."@en ;
