    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete: use HPLO] Composite of 'Corton Formation': very silty, sandy clay or clayey sand, commonly laminated; with few pebbles and sand lenses, and 'Lowestoft Formation': primarily a stiff, bluish-grey clay when fresh; orange-brown to brown where weathered; with varying amounts of chalk, flint, silt and sand. Derived mostly from Jurassic and Cretaceous strata. [Generic description: from East Anglian data]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QA> ;
