    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete: use MAHO] A grey, fine-grained, slightly bioclastic,well-bedded limestone with a sandy base, and interpreted to be of marine origin, containing brachiopods and rare rugose corals, crinoids, and commonly  Zoophycus caudagalli trace fossils."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally a conformable change from a rooted sandstone within the Lower Limestone Formation lying about 20m above the Middle (and Upper Skateraw) Limestone (now named the Blackhall Limestone)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CX> ;
