    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Complex landslide deposits are formed by landslides which exhibit at least two types of movement (falling, toppling, sliding, flowing, spreading) in sequence. Many landslips are complex, although one type of movement may dominate over the others at certain areas within a slide or at a particular time (for example: rockfall-debris flow)."@en ;
