        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Well-sorted fine- to medium-grained micaceus sand, generally up to about 11 m thick but locally up to more than 80 m in the Stradbroke Trough. Its sedimentology indicates that it formed in an intertidal environment."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Overlies the Crag 'Stone-bed'  comprised predominantly of flints and phosphate nodules, or is unconformable on Chalk. There is a sharp lithological change across junction."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.58e+00 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Generally up to about 11 m but up to over 80 m in the Stradbroke Trough."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Overlain locally by College Farm Member, Kesgrave Formation or Lowestoft Formation. Junction is easily determined  by change in lithology."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 0e+00 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:NCG ;
    skos:definition "Sand with subsidiary silt. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Quaternary Period (2.58-0 Ma BP)."@en ;
