namedrockunit:DAIN
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/A> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CALSPL"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEMPG"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SPQM"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Formation comprises a lower calcareous semipelite unit succeeded by a massive schistose garnet-mica semipelite that constitutes the dominant lithology in the formation. The lower calcareous unit comprises 0 to 30m of calcareous garnet-mica schist and muscovite-quartz schist; extremely pitted weathering is conspicuous. The calcareous unit is succeeded by massive, poorly bedded garnet-mica schist and muscovite-quartz schist, poor in biotite but with abundant quartz sweats. Garnets are typically 1-2mm across, commonly chloritised and wrapped by muscovite. The unit is typically resistant to weathering and commonly forms brown-weathering cliffs 5 to 10m high."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Change from white-weathering pinkish-brown quartzose psammite and quartzite of the preceding Beinn a'Chaisteil Quartzite Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AC> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 7.2e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AC> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Sections through the formation on Beinn a'Chaisteil and in Allt Coire an Lochain suggest of the order of 70m where not intensely folded. Contrast this with a thickness of at least 350m exposed in the back wall of Coire an Lochain on Beinn 'a Chreachain. In Coire Daingean the unit is 120 to 140m, again probably thickened by folding."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Change to the alternating muscovite-rich semipelite, psammite and quartzite of the Beinn an Dothaidh Heterolithic Formation. A calcareous semipelite or calcsilicate-rock (c.5m thick) may be present at the base of the succeeding unit."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AC> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 6.35e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:DALO ;
    skos:definition "Garnet semipelite and quartz-muscovite semipelite with subsidiary calcareous semipelite. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Cryogenian Period (Precambrian) (720-635 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "DAIN"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Coire Daingean Semipelite Formation"@en ;
.

