    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Pale grey, pink and white, flaggy to blocky, thin- to thick-bedded, siliceous and feldspathic psammite, locally with thin muscovite-rich beds and laminae. Subordinate quartzite beds common. Micaceous psammite and thin semipelite beds also present. Locally distinctive beds of interbanded psammitic and semipelitic gneiss, with quartz-feldspar augen and veins."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Passes downwards into more mixed psammites and semipelites, locally gneissose. Possibly locally shear zone boundary. Onlap of Upper Devonian sediments obscures lower contacts in parts."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1e+03 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 3000m, and possibly thicker."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Passes up with gradational contact up into the Knockando Quartzite Formation over much of its outcrop. Truncated to the north-east by the Rothes Fault, and North-east of this structure possibly equivalent to undefined psammite and quartzite units within the Grampian Group."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 5.41e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:GRAM ;
    skos:definition "Psammite with subsidiary quartzite and trace semipelite. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Neoproterozoic Era (Precambrian) (1000-541 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "DAPS"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dallas Psammite Formation"@en ;
.

