    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use TCON] \r
\r
Variable lithology. Matrix-supported or matrix-rich accumulation of rock fragments of any size or shape at the foot of a gully or chute in a cliff or steep slope. Formed by mass movement - rainwash, sheetwash, debris flow, mudslide or avalanche. May be active or inactive. [Generic description: 'TMOS' Procedures]."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.58e+00 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
