    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Consists mainly of hard, white conglomerates with subordinate pebbly sandstones with a few lenses of purplish-grey/grey mudstone up to 30cm thick. Trough cross-bedding is common in sets from 0.2m to 1.0m thick. Many of the units are upward fining in grain size. The clasts and pebbles are almost exclusively of vein quartz and well-rounded, averaging 2cm but up to 10cm in diameter, but some blocks of sandstone up to 15cm across are also present. Palaeocurrent directions indicate transport of the original sediments towards the southsouthwest."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Drawn at the base of the conglomerate of the Douglas Muir Quartz Conglomerate where it rests apparently unconformably on volcaniclastic sediments of the Kirkwood Formation, as at a natural exposure at NS 5307 7752."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CX> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.309e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CX> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "20m at the type locality at Douglas Muir Quarry, and up to 70m maximum elsewhere."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The boundary is transistional, as seen at a natural exposure at NS 5730 7774, by upward passage by interbedding from conglomerate to white and pale grey sandstones of the Craigmaddie Muir Sandstones of the Lawmuir Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CX> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.303e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:LWM ;
    skos:definition "Conglomerate with subsidiary mudstone and pebbly (gravelly) sandstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Brigantian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (330.9-330.3 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "DMQ"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Douglas Muir Quartz-Conglomerate Member"@en ;
.

