        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Dark grey, partly calcareous, siltstone and mudstone, with thin beds, lenticles or nodules of silty limestone.  Poorly fossiliferous sandier beds occur near the top and base; at the base these include debris from the Borrowdale Volcanic Group with the commonly occuring brachiopod Trematis corona ['corona facies']"@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at the base of sandstones and siltstones of the 'corona facies', overlying volcaniclastic rocks of the Harthwaite Formation [Borrowdale Volcanic Group]"@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/O4> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 4.582e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "About 400m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Overlain by limestones of the Swindale or Keisley limestone formations, or where these are absent, the Ashgill Formation"@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/OA> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.431e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:DNT ;
    skos:definition "Calcareous siltstone and siltstone with subsidiary calcareous mudstone and limestone and trace sandstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Caradoc Series - to - Ashgill Series (Ordovician Period) (458.2-443.1 Ma BP)."@en ;
