        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLMDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Limestone, pale grey, micritised, sparsely bioclastic crinoidal packstone with wisps and disrupted layers of yellow silty shale."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Either gradational, with normal limestones of the formation (ie downward decrease in micritisation) or abrupt, with base marked by 0.06 - 0.2m layer of grey shales and noduler limestones; also rests on Drumowen Sandstone and Crockanaver Limestone members."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
