namedrockunit:ESHET
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use SHEGR] Name introduced by Gillespie et al. (2011) for major intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite (SHEGR) that occur east of the Walls Boundary Fault. Intrusions of the Shetland Islands Suite are apparently temporally distinct on either side of the fault. \r
\r
Term not currently used by BGS."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/S> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 4.431e+02 ;
