    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Ferricrete is a type of duricrust. It is a conglomerate consisting of surficial sand and gravel cemented into a hard mass by iron oxide derived from the oxidation of percolating solutions of iron salts. Synonyms: iron laterite, iron pan."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.58e+00 ;
