    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Gneissose, locally migmatitic semipelite with minor quartzite. Quartzite is more common near contacts with adjacent units."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Transitional with the Beinn Bhreac Psammite Formation (BBPS); incoming of first persistent quartzite layer. No way-up criteria."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AT> ;
