        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLTE"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Purple and green slates with silty laminations in the central part of the outcrop. Grey slates with local spilite lavas (some pillow structures), bluish-grey calcareous siltstones between Bremridge and Farlacombe ]SX 792 711] and buff siltstone to the south-east of Bickington are seen to the north-west and south-east. Rare ferruginous or siliceous nodules occur throughout the formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Undefined."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DR> ;
