    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Harwich Stone Band is a tabular argillaceous limestone with a central ash bed, that occurs near the base of the clayey silts and silty clays in the lower part of the Wrabness Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GY> ;
