        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Kame terrace deposits refer to a landform deposited continuously along a valley side, by the meltwater at the junction between the valley side and an ice mass. It consists of stratified sand and gravel, and the outer edge may display collapse features."@en ;
