namedrockunit:KEST
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Defined by Gibbard and Preece (pp. 59-60 in Bowen, 1999) to include the fluvial and associated gravel terrace deposits of the River Stour. They defined the Chislet Member (pre-Devensian), Folkestone Battery Bed (faunal evidence suggests correlation with the Ipswichian, MIS 5e stage) and Kennington Member (Devensian). BGS maps show up to 10 aggradations above the alluvium."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QO> ;
