    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Porphyritic olivine-basalt lava. Neither top, nor base is exposed in the Langholm District. As described in the Langholm memoir it is unclear whether associated \"sediments\" are interbedded with or below the basalt at the type locality of Kershope Quarry, but they  probably sit at the base of the basalt. The lithology of the KHB is therefore defined only as olivine-basalt."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Not seen but presumed to be conformable with sedimentary rocks of the Fell Sandstone Formation. Underlain by sedimentary strata, mainly sandstones of the Fell Sandstone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CQ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.43e+02 ;
