        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLMDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The unit comprises soft grey to greenish grey mudstones and silty mudstones with subordinate thin beds of siltstone, clay ironstone, sandstone and limestone. In some areas, where the Cuckfield Stone Bed is absent, the upper and lower Grinstead Clay cannot be separated."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base is taken at the up-section change from sandstone (Tunbridge Wells Sand Formation, Ardingley Sandstone Member, which may include at its top the Top Lower Tunbridge Wells Pebble Bed) to silty mudstones of the lower Grinstead Clay."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KV> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.377e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KV> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/U> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 6.4m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary is taken at an up-section change from mudstones to sandstones of the (Cuckfield Stone Member). Where the Cuckfield Stone Bed is absent, the upper and lower Grinstead Clay cannot be separated."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KV> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.326e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:GRC ;
    skos:definition "Mudstone with subsidiary siltstone and silty mudstone and trace limestone and sandstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Valanginian Age (Cretaceous Period) (137.7-132.6 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "LGRC"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Lower Grinstead Clay"@en ;
