        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Packages between 15 and 30m thick of pale brown, argillaceous to sandy limestone, displaying turbiditic facies, normal graded with sharp bases, interbedded with thinner sequences of pyritic and carbonaceous mudstone and thin sandstone beds."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base of the lowest thick, pale brown turbiditic limestone package, where it rests on grey-brown calcareous mudstones and limestones of the Long Eaton Formation."@en ;
