    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Lodgement till is, usually overconsolidated, geotechnically stiff to hard till. It has been formed beneath a glacier as successive layers of glacial debris (ill-sorted rock flour and gravel to boulder grade, generally referred to as diamicton) plastered upon bedrock or other glacial deposits, by pressure melting and/or other mechanical processes."@en ;
