        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEMPEL"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "An undifferentiated, regularly bedded sequence of banded to laminated psammite, with thick units of semipelite and some pelite. Decimetre-scale beds of impure quartzite are common close to the base of the overlying unit, seen as part of the transitional change upwards. Pebbly and gritty beds are uncommon, and cross-lamination is rarely seen."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Undefined, not yet mapped."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1e+03 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Unknown."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Boundary defined on first occurrence of grey to white quartzite."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 5.41e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:GRAM ;
    skos:definition "Psammite with subsidiary pelite and semipelite and trace pebbly psammite. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Neoproterozoic Era (Precambrian) (1000-541 Ma BP)."@en ;
