        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Heterogeneous silts, sands and clays. The bulk of the member is composed of red, soft silty clays, laminated reddish or grey clays and silty fine-grained sands with a few scattered pebbles. It includes bodies of reddish brown, Trias-rich till, similar to the Thrussington Till Member (THT), and the silts are analogous to the Wolston Clay Member (WOC) of the Avon Valley and Leicestershire."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.58e+00 ;
