namedrockunit:NBRG
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/DMTN"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use CALI] \r
\r
The group comprises all formations and lithogenetic units of glacigenic deposits of Oxygen Isotope Stage 6 equivalent and younger. These deposits commonly form the surface deposits of northern Britain and are mainly confined to land lying to the north of the main Devensian ice sheet limit. Being the products of the latest glaciations the deposits commonly have distinct morphological expression and this morphology may form an important part of the definition of component formations and offspring units. Lithologies are diamicton, gravel, sand, silt and clay. \r
\r
Provisional term in draft framework (equivalent of Northern Britain Glacigenic Group of McMillan and Hamblin, 2000); Devensian glacigenic deposits reassigned to the Caledonia Glacigenic Group (CALI)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Unconformable on bedrock of Neogene age or older, locally unconformable on older Quaternary deposits."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H3269 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QO> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.62e-01 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/G> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "To 200m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Conformable or unconformable contact with non-glacigenic deposits of Late Devensian and Holocene age."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.18e-02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> ;
    skos:altLabel "Newer Drift [Obsolete: use CALI, NBRG]"@en ;
    skos:definition "Obsolete name. Clay, diamicton, gravel, sand and silt. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Wolstonian Stage - to - Devensian Stage (Quaternary Period) (.362-.0118 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "NBRG"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "North Britain Glacigenic Group [Obsolete: use CALI]"@en ;
.

