        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEMPEL"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Pale to dark grey, buff weathering, flaggy, feldspathic psammite, with subsidiary micaceous psammite, semipelite and quartzite. Locally more micaceous in parts and also contains thick quartzite beds. Lenticular calc-silicate pods widespread but not abundant in the psammites."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Presumed gradational boundary with underlying siliceous psammites, quartzites and graded psammites, semipelites and pelites of Pityoulish Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1e+03 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "2000 to 5000m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Grades upwards and laterally into siliceous psammites and quartzites of the Knockando Quartzite Formation, and into psammite and quartzite members of the Tormore Psammite Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 5.41e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:GRAM ;
    skos:definition "Psammite with subsidiary micaceous psammite, quartzite and semipelite and trace calcsilicate-rock. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Neoproterozoic Era (Precambrian) (1000-541 Ma BP)."@en ;
