        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Prestwich Formation consists of an alternation of fine to medium grained sandstones with green-grey to grey-green silty mudstones. Two sandstone units are present. The lower sandstone displays wireline-log signatures indicative of upward coarsening, whereas the upper sandstone possess a sharp base and displays a more or less consistent log character."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GL> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 4.81e+01 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "The Prestwich Formation is about 450 m thick in well 49/1-2."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GI> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.39e+01 ;
