namedrockunit:PSTN
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/J> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CAMDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LMST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use POST] \r
\r
Variable sandy marine limestones commonly with large and robust molluscan macrofauna, such as the Aylesbury Limestone, Rubbly Limestone, Cockly Bed, Creamy Limestone  and Town Gardens Limestone) and variable calcareous sands and sandstones, generally non-glauconitic such as the  Crendon Sand, Swindon Sand and Swindon Sandstone."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Upward transition from variable calcareous and glauconitic sand or sandstone such as the Portland Sand Member, to variable sandy limestone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JI> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.492e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JI> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to, and locally greater than 11 m thick."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Upward change from fully marine limestones with large molluscan fossils of Portland Stone Member to lagoonal fine-grained limestones and marls of Purbeck Formation (the base of which is commonly Marked either by laminated, ostracod-bearing 'Pendle' or oyster-bearing marl, or by a sharp non-sequential contact with overlying, generally non-calcareous and commonly ferruginous sands and sandstones of the Lower Greensand or Whitchurch Sand Formation, or by calcareous mudstones of the Gault Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JI> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.431e+02 ;
    lexicon:isObsoleteEquivalentOf namedrockunit:POST ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> ;
    skos:altLabel "Portland Stone Formation"@en ;
    skos:definition "Obsolete name. Limestone, sand and sandstone with subsidiary calcareous mudstone and mudstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Tithonian Age (Jurassic Period) (149.2-143.1 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "PSTN"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Portland Stone Member (Wiltshire, Oxfordshire and Buckinghamshire) [Obsolete: use POST]"@en ;
.

