namedrockunit:REDF
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/S> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Mainly red mudstones and sandstones exposed on the cliffs and rocky foreshore at the northern end of Albion Sands [SM 771 077]. The formation comprises red to purple mudstones/siltstones and red, purple and greyish pink, typically fine-grained sandstones. \r
\r
Dryland alluvial environments with deposition in low-sinuosity ephemeral sand-bed channels, point bar lateral accretion and unconfined sheetfloods. The mudstones represent floodplain deposits subjected to pedogenic vertisol development as well as fluvial deposition of mud aggregates (Hillier and Williams, 2004). \r
\r
Hillier and Williams (2004) reported a late Ludfordian age based on a trilete spore assemblage."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "At the type section, the lower boundary is conformable, where the basal red mudstones of the Red Cliff Formation rest on grey deltaic deposits of the Gray Sandstone Formation (Hillier, 2000; Hillier and Williams, 2004). At Red Cliff, calcretised red mudstones interdigitate with grey sandstones with inclined heterolithic stratification of the Gray Sandstone Formation (Hillier, 2000)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SD> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 4.25e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SD> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Thicknesses range from 17 m at Lindsway Bay and 50 m at Albion Sands to 55 m at the type section of Red Cliff (Hillier and Williams, 2004)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary is placed at the top of red mudstones, where they are overlain by pale quartz-rich sandstones of the Albion Sands Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SD> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.227e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:MIH ;
    skos:definition "Mudstone and sandstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Ludfordian Age (Silurian Period) (425-422.7 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "REDF"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Red Cliff Formation"@en ;
.

