    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Limestone, brown-grey, arenaceous biosparite, oolite, interbedded with calcareous, fine-grained, cross-bedded and parallel laminated feldspathic sandstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Not exposed but by analogy with its lateral equivalent the Gortnaree Sandstone Member, it succeeds conformably, and abruptly, the Termon River Limestone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CI> ;
