namedrockunit:RSLD
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Rotational slides are a type of slide characterised by movement along a curved, concave-upwards failure surface; this imparts a back-tilt or into-slope dip to the slipped mass which thus sinks at the rear and heaves at the toe."@en ;
