        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Brownish grey (Munsell Soil) sandy silt with shell fragments and diverse assemblages of cold water marine dinoflagellate cysts and foraminifera."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Gradational, conformable contact with dark brown, calcareous, laminated silt and clay of the Carleton Hall Clay Member of the Glannoventia Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.16e-01 ;
