\r
Head, scree and slope wash deposits, covering upland areas. These include boulder scree, and some 'redeposited' gravels and diamictons. The head and scree deposits intercalate with glacigenic sediments of the Orrisdale Formation at low elevations around the island margin."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally unconformable on bedrock, except where the head and scree deposits interdigitate with glacigenic sediments of the Orrisdale Formation."@en ;
