        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SISTCC"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sandstone, grey, mostly weathered orange-brown, fine- to medium-grained siliceous with ganister levels particularly near top. Delta top sandstone. 0.2m coal at reference section, c 12m from top of unit."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Not exposed but as delta top sandstone overlies delta slope deposits of the Roeburndale Member, likely to be sharp and erosional on siltstones with thin sandstones."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CG> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.27e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CG> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/B> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "12m+ in Sapling Clough (basal part not seen). c.12m in tributary to Foxdale Beck (basal and top parts not seen)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Sharp with c 0.5m grey micaceous sandy siltstone overlain by claystones of the Eumorpoceras yatesae Marine Band."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CG> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.2375e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:RBL ;
    skos:definition "Sandstone with subsidiary ganister and trace coal. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Arnsbergian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (327-323.75 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "SPCS"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sapling Clough Sandstone"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:SPE
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CH"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Soft to firm to very stiff, highly to moderately plastic, sandy, silty clay with shells and pebbles. Some clay and numerous sand/silt lenses may give a laminated appearance. Similar in geotechnical strength to underlying clay but more uniform colour/less streaky and has more pebbles and shells. Geotechnically weaker and more uniform than overlying till-like unit."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Lower boundary is a strong seismic reflector in otherwise parallel or sub parallel reflectors above and below in the Cape Shore Formation with which it is apparently conformable."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QMIS002> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.4e-02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QMIS002> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "40 metres from seismic sections. Thins to west where it crops out. Absent in the Norwegian Trench area where it has been eroded or never deposited."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary is also apparently conformable with the Tampen Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QMIS002> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.39e-02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:REAP ;
    skos:definition "Clay with subsidiary shelly clay and trace sand and silt. Stratified bedrock. Occurs offshore. Deposited during the Marine Isotope Stage 2 (Quaternary Period) (.024-.0139 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "SPE"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sperus Formation"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:SPEK
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Heterolithic, varicoloured, but usually green or grey, unit of sandstones, siltstones and mudstones."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary is defined by the downward change from varicoloured, but usually green or grey, heterolithic sediments to red Triassic sediments (Cormorant Formation). A weak down-section increase in gamma values coincides with the boundary."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JH> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.014e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to c. 100 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top is marked by a sharp downward change from sandstone dominated, coal-bearing strata (Fladen Group) to argillaceous, coal-free deposits. The boundary coincides with a sharp down-section increase in gamma values."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JT> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.747e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:DUNL ;
    skos:definition "Mudstone, sandstone and siltstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs offshore. Deposited during the Hettangian Age - to - Toarcian Age (Jurassic Period) (201.4-174.7 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "SPEK"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Speke Formation"@en ;
