namedrockunit:SWCB
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """The Swanscombe Member comprises glauconitic, very silty or sandy clays, sandy silts and sandy clayey silts, which may contain dispersed shells and lignite. It is highly glauconitic and locally gravelly at the base. Ash particles occur in the Swanscombe Member in south-west Essex (Knox, 1983).\r
King (1981) observes that the unit is similar in lithology to the Oldhaven Member, specifically in its western facies (his Tilehurst Member), but that where the units coexist there is a discontinuity between them usually marked by a gravel bed. Also, the fauna differs."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The glauconitic clays and silts of the Swanscombe Member rests on the glauconitic sands silts and clays of the Oldhaven Member, or the Lambeth Group, on a sharp, erosive contact, commonly marked by flint gravel."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GY> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 5.6e+01 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GY> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Thin (less than 2 m) or absent in the western London Basin, north Kent and the Hampshire Basin. Elsewhere in the London Basin thickens northwards to more than 10 m (King, 1981)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top of the Swanscombe Member is marked by an upwards change from glauconitic clays and silts to non-glauconitic silty clay, some sandy, some gravelly, of the Walton Member (London Clay Formation)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GY> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.81e+01 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:HWH ;
    skos:definition "Clay and silt. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Ypresian Age (Palaeogene Period) (56-48.1 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "SWCB"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Swanscombe Member"@en ;
.

