    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """See TILL Till. Till, 1 is older than Till in the same map area. \r
\r
Group of sediments laid down by the direct action of glacial ice. Variable lithology, usually sandy, silty clay (possibly chalky in southeast England) with pebbles, but can contain gravel-rich, or laminated sand layers; varied colour and consistency. [Generic description]."""@en ;
