    skos:definition "Rhyolite lava and tuff with subsidiary lapillistone, mudstone, sandstone and volcaniclastic-breccia. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Ediacaran Period (Precambrian) - to - Comley Series (Cambrian Period) (635-508 Ma BP)."@en ;
