        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CSSST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Conglomerate, matrix-clast supported, calcareous, very coarse sand (grit) matrix. Clasts up to 6cm, unsorted, rounded/subrounded, exclusively of white, milky and clear vein quartz."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Within Bin Mountain Sandstone: Change from orange-weathering, fine-grained sandstones, below, to coarse conglomerate."@en ;
