namedrockunit:UBB
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/S> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LMST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Light olive-grey, irregularly bedded, flaggy and nodular silty limestones, frequently crinoidal. \r
\r
The benthic fauna includes large brachiopods, tabulate corals and stromatoporoids. Coquinas of the brachiopod Kirkidium knightii (J. Sowerby) are characteristic (the K. knightii Association), particularly in more western outcrops (Holland et al., 1963; Lawson and White, 1989; Watkins and Aithie, 1980)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "An increase in the proportion of harder limestone to calcareous siltstone distinguishes the Upper Bringewood Formation from the underlying Lower Bringewood Formation (LBN)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SG> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 4.267e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SG> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "The formation is estimated to be between 12 and 45 m thick."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The base of the overlying Lower Leintwardine Formation (LLT) is defined on faunal rather than lithological criteria, i.e. above the highest occurrences of Kirkidium knightii (J. Sowerby), Strophonella euglypha (Hisinger) and tabulate corals, and therefore at the faunal change from the Mesopholidostrophia laevigata Association to the Sphaerirhynchia wilsoni Association."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SG> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.25e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:definition "Limestone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Gorstian Age (Silurian Period) (426.7-425 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:isTopConceptOf lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "UBB"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Upper Bringewood Formation"@en ;
.

