        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "From about 9 km from Stedham, West Sussex [SU 86 22] to east of Selham, West Sussex [SU 94 20] the Fittleworth Member is divided by the Selham Ironshot Member. Samuel (1994) proposed the name 'Upper Fittleworth Beds' for the upper division (c. 2 m thick). This is re-named informally the 'upper Fittleworth Member', with the lower division (to c. 8 m) named the 'lower Fittleworth Member'."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KP> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.214e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KP> ;
