    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "152m in eastern Mendip, thinning westwards to a feather edge in the central Mendip Hills."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Taken at incoming of ooidal limestones and crinoidal/ooidal limestones of the overlying Burrington Oolite Subgroup above the coarse crinoidal limestone of the Formation. Little is known about this contact, which needs further investigation. At the type locality it is taken at the incoming of calcite mudstones and ooidal/crinoidal limestones of the overlying Clifton Down Limestone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
