    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete: use WDH] Pale lilac or pink trachytes and andesites with phenocrysts of biotite and alkali-feldspars, principally sanidine in a fluidal matrix or laths of sanidine with patches of haematite and secondary grains of quartz."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Drawn at the base of trachytes, acid andesites and other silicified acid rocks of the Woodhouselee Group where it conformably rests upon rhyolites, acid tuffs, trachyte and andesite of the Caerketton Group."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DL> ;
