namedrockunit:WYSL
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLTE"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete: use WWYM] Whiteway Slate consists predominantly of grey-black, green and purple slates that are locally calcareous and siliceous, and rarely sideritic. The Slates contain a rich planktonic fauna of ammonoids, ostracods and conodonts; benthic fauna include crinoid debris and brachiopods, among others; ammonoids are rare except in the nodule-rich facies of the Chudleigh escarpment."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Conformable with the underlying Luxton Nodular Limestone; the transition between this lithologies is marked by the change from nodular and laminated limestones of the Luxton Nodular Limestone to the predominance of grey-black, green and purple slates of the Whiteway Slates, which are locally calcareous and siliceous and rarely sideritic."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DA> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.711e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 120 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary of the Whiteway Slate in the Ugbrooke Unit (i.e. the thickness of rock that is bounded by the Bickington Thrust in the north and the Ware Barton Thrust in the south) is taken to be below the lowest of the sooty black shales that are placed within the Winstow Slate; in the field this transition would be identified by the change from grey-black, green and purple slates of the Whiteway Slate (described in the lithology section above) to the siliceous and sooty shales of the Winstow Slate, the basal part of the Winstow Chert, (green or greyish green, black and purple cherts) which is not separately mappable."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CT> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.467e+02 ;
    lexicon:isObsoleteEquivalentOf namedrockunit:WWYM ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> ;
    skos:altLabel "Whiteway Mudstone Formation"@en ;
    skos:definition "Obsolete name. Slate. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Famennian Age (Devonian Period) - to - Tournaisian Age (Carboniferous Period) (371.1-346.7 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "WYSL"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Whiteway Slate Formation [Obsolete: use WWYM]"@en ;
.

