namedrockunit:ZELD
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/DOLMST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Zeeland Formation in well 53/12-2 comprises 300 m of pale brown to dark brown, microcrystalline and very finely crystalline dolomitic limestone, with occasional oolitic beds, overlying 150 m of dark brown and dark grey, finely crystalline dolomite. In the Somerton No.1 well (East Anglia), partly equivalent mid to late Dinantian limestones contain partings of grey mudstone, and have fossiliferous beds containing abundant corals, brachiopods, bivalves, bryozoans and crinoids."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Dinantian carbonates of the East Midlands Shelf generally rest on deformed Lower Paleozoic basinal-marine and volcaniclastic sediments (Strank, 1987). In the Somerton No.1 well, however, the carbonates overlie a local development of mid-Dinantian sandstones and mudstones. The base of the Zeeland Formation has not been drilled in the UK sector, but the formation is known to rest on Upper Devonian clastic sediments (Famenne Shale) in parts of the southern Netherlands."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CF> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.593e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "53/12-2 penetrated 450 m of Dinantian carbonates where seismic suggests > 1000 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top of the Zeeland Formation is a regional unconformity. Its boundary with overlying late Namurian or Westphalian fluviodeltaic sediments (Millstone Grit Formation or Westoe Coal Formation) is a clearly defined lithological transition, marked by a sharp downhole decrease in gamma-ray response and increase in velocity (e.g. 53/12-2)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CX> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.303e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:CL ;
    skos:definition "Dolomitic limestone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs offshore. Deposited during the Courceyan Substage - to - Brigantian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (359.3-330.3 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "ZELD"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Zeeland Formation"@en ;
.

