    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "c. 550-650 m (based on outcrop width with no allowance for probable folding)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Top of highest persistent metabasalt sheet. Background lithology changes from greywacke grits with pelites to persistent pelites of the Corinacy Pelite Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
