    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "To c.35m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top is taken at the top of highest chert or siliceous mudstone of the Formation, where it is overlain by the lowest quartzite of the Twrch Sandstone Formation. In the partial type section of the Kenfig Borehole, the top is not seen, the Formation being unconformably overlain by marl and red clay of the Mercia Mudstone Group at 12.8m depth."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CG> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.2375e+02 ;
