        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A mostly pale yellowish brown pebbly sand, containing a relatively large proportion of pink granite and seams of chocolate brown or dark grey clay, which is interpreted as having been derived from the underlying Pitlurg Till Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "A sharp, undulating, erosional, unconformable contact with dark grey, pebbly clay diamicton of the Pitlurg Till Formation."@en ;
