namedrockunit:BAST
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BA"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Baston Burn Lava Member consists predominantly of plagioclase-macrophyric basalt lavas (of 'Markle' type) with a few microporphyritic lavas, or microporphyritic components of composite lavas (of 'Jedburgh' type)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "In the northern Touch Hills, and north-eastern Gargunnock Hills, the basal macroporphyritic lava of the member is conformable or disconformable on a trachybasalt lava of the Slackdown Lava Member. Farther west, where the trachybasalt is absent, the basal lava of the Baston Burn Lava Member is a transitional plagioclase-macrophyric to plagioclase-microphyric basalt which overlies conformably or disconformably a microporphyritic basalt of the Slackdown Lava Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H40 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.445e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "9-67 m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "In the northern Touch Hills and north-eastern Gargunnock Hills, the Baston Burn Lava Member is overlain unconformably by the Spout of Ballochleam Lava Member, and the Baston Burn Lava Member is progressively truncated towards the west. The lithological change is to microporphyritic basalt (of 'Jedburgh' type). In the north-western Gargunnock Hills, the Baston Burn Lava Member is overlain unconformably by the Slackgun Volcaniclastic Member, and the lithological transition is to weathered basalt ('bole') and well-bedded tuff."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CR> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.309e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel "Baston Burn Group [Obsolete: use BAST]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:CPV ;
    skos:definition "Basalt. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Arundian Substage - to - Asbian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (344.5-330.9 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "BAST"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Baston Burn Lava Member"@en ;
.

