        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/VCSR"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Volcaniclastic sedimentary rock, some lacustrine, tuff and agglomerate. Pyroclastic rocks include tephra cones which in some places coalesce. Lacustrine sedimentary rocks in the form of mudstone containing fish scales, overlying a discontinuous coal seam, are exposed south of Rigangower [NS 438 757]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The Burncrooks Volcaniclastic Member is underlain by the sedimentary rocks of the Clyde Sandstone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H45 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
