    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use SMCL] \r
\r
Diamicton, comprising massive silty clayey sand with scattered pebbles of flint, sandstone, etc. containing rafts of chalk and bodies of "marly drift" (reconstituted chalk), interbedded with sands and laminated clays. (Age OIS 10 or 12)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Rests upon the Lowestoft Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H687 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QB> ;
