        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sandstone, protoquartzitic, in sharp-based medium-bedded units with some preserved sole marks on the bases of units, and mudstone with ironstone beds and nodules.  Soft sediment deformation structures common in places."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary is taken at the base of the first protoquartzitic sandstone-dominated unit above black fissile mudstone that includes a Hodsonites magistrorum Marine Band."@en ;
