    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Planar thin-bedded to ripple-cross laminated volcaniclastic siltstone and fine-grained volcaniclastic sandstone; some intercalated coarse-grained volcaniclastic sandstone containing elongate pumice fragments."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at the base of well bedded volcaniclastic rocks generally overlying the Pavey Ark Breccia Member, but in places overlapping the Scafell Dacite and volcaniclastic breccia of the Cam Crags Member"@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H3209 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/O4> ;
