    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Mudstone and siltstone, shaly and micaceous, red to purplish in colour but bleached white in places. Considered to be \"argillised ash\" by Mortimore et al., (2001). Organic-rich and sandy in lower part."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary is unconformable above an erosive contact with underlying conglomerates of the Clach Alasdair Conglomerate Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H697 ;
