    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete: use CHAM] Mainly grey mudstones; includes scattered calcite mudstone nodules, and several continuous beds with abundant nodules of calcite mudstone, phosphate or siderite mudstone: also in type area two thin limestone beds, calcareous siltstone bed, and basal thin ferruginous oolite."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Erosive, non-sequential contact of Glebe Farm Bed with underlying Scunthorpe Mudstone Formation in type area. In north Lincolnshire, at top of Frodingham Ironstone."@en ;
