    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 150 m thick at Callander, 50m at Beinn Liath [NN 578 040], and 2 m near Gartmore."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "A gradational contact with an overlying reddish grey, coarse- to fine-grained, locally pebbly, and commonly massive sandstone, of the undivided Ruchill Flagstone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DL> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.943e+02 ;
