    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Clifton Rock consists of up to three leaves of fine-grained cross-bedded or ripple cross-laminated sandstone and includes a thin coal. The Shertcliffe Coal rests on the top leaf, sometimes termed the Shertcliffe Seatstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CA> ;
