    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Corrie Lava Member consists of plagioclase-macrophyric basalt and trachybasalt lavas (of 'Markle' type), aphyric basaltic-trachandesite (mugearite) lavas, and lapilli-tuff and tuff-breccia beds. Derivation is thought to be from local vents (Craig, 1980)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The Corrie Lava Member is fault-bounded and the lower boundary is not seen."@en ;
