    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Cross-bedded sandstones and sandy limestones comprise most of the Member.  These are commonly either massive or thinly bedded and contain crinoid ossicles, bivalves, bryzoan, belemnites and brachiopod fragments, especially in the lower part of the succession. Limited to Straithaird peninsula, intense lateral variation."@en ;
