    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Fine-to medium-grained sand with stringers of granule gravel and channels containing clast-supported gravel. The gravel comprises subangular to subrounded clasts of Skiddaw Group sandstones and siltstones, red and yellow sandstone, Borrowdale Volcanic Group rocks, granite, granophyre, coal and ironstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally undulating erosional contact on to Drigg Beach Till Member of the Gosforth Glacigenic Formation."@en ;
