        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEMPEL"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Psammite and micaceous psammite, grey and flaggy, with thin micaceous partings. To the east of the A9 road typically grey to pink quartzose psammite and interbanded psammite and micaceous psammite with prominent calc-silicate rock concretions. Minor units of semipelite, locally with associated thin quartzite beds."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Not seen."@en ;
