    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use TPSF] \r
\r
Red-brown siltstones, thinly interlayered with very fine- to fine-grained sandstones and mudstones. Ripple marks, halite pseudomorphs, micaceous surfaces common."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Where a dominantly arenaceous sequence passes up into a dominantly argillaceous sequence (locally conformable on the Hawksmoor Formation)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H4008 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/TA> ;
