        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/QZITE"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Hornblende schist, fine-grained with layers and lenses of hornblende psammite. Interfingers with the Ben Lawers Schist Formation in the east of outcrop and locally with intercalated psammite in the upper parts of the Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Base of dominantly fine-grained amphibolitic succession overlying the Ben Lawers Schist Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:DBFB ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1e+03 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Generally 200 to 300m, although thicker in the Ben Vrackie area [NN 94 63]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Gradational boundary with Ben Lui Schist Formation located where psammite and semipelite become the dominant lithology."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 5.41e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
