namedrockunit:FORCA
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/P"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Includes the fluvial and related organic deposits of the catchments surrounding the Forth Estuary. \r
\r
The deposits include alluvium and river terrace deposits comprising gravel, sand, silt and peat. Rock types are principally of Carboniferous and Devonian strata (sandstone, siltstone) with volcanic (basalt and andesite) and intrusive igneous rocks (microdiorite) of Midland Valley provenance. Variable but generally minor components of Dalradian metasedimentary and Caledonian igneous rocks derived from the Grampian Highlands are present. \r
\r
A suite of fluvial (alluvium and river terrace deposits) and associated organic and lacustrine sediments that contain clasts derived from Palaeozoic rocks and glacigenic deposits cropping out in the catchment of the River Forth and other rivers flowing directly to the Firth of Forth, including the rivers Teith, Almond, Carron, Allan Water, and the rivers Esk and Tyne of the Lothians. \r
\r
Late Devensian to Holocene (MIS 2-1)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Unconformable contact with units of the Midland Valley, Mearns and Central Grampian Glacigenic subgroups and bedrock."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.16e-01 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/UG> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 25 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Generally the ground surface, but units of the subgroup may be overlain locally by mass movement deposits or may locally interfinger with units of the British Coastal Deposits Group."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QH> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 0e+00 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:BCAT ;
    skos:definition "Gravel and sand with subsidiary clay, peat and silt. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devensian Stage - to - Holocene Epoch (Quaternary Period) (.116-0 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:narrower namedrockunit:FOVA ;
    skos:notation "FORCA"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Forth Catchments Subgroup"@en ;
.

