        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LMST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Chalk, with some flint bands and \"incipient flints\". Marl partings common towards the base, with some glauconite."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The exact relationship with the underlying Cloghfin Sponge Formation is uncertain (Fletcher, 1977, p.8, paragraph 2). The lower boundary is taken at a well-developed separation plane above which the beds contain no appreciable arenaceous \"contamination\"."@en ;
