        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A dark grey mudstone, with pale siltstone laminae and quartz arenite sandstone as thin to medium beds locally forming packets up to several tens of metres; debrite (pebbly mudstone) locally in the south becoming extensive in the north."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "In stratigraphical contact with the Barrule Formation.at the base, which is marked by a change from a mudstone-dominated to a mudstone/sandstone facies"@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H2860 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/OR> ;
