    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """The Kentish Sands Member mostly comprises silty fine-grained sand, becoming more clayey downwards. It is mainly non-calcareous. \r
\r
Probably early to mid-Thanetian in age, based on dinoflagellate cysts and its inferred lateral passage into the upper part of the Pegwell Silt Member (King, in prep.)."""@en ;
