        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete: use BSG] Mudstone, dark grey to black, blocky or shaly, calcareous, pyritic, petroliferous, with subordinate interbedded limestones and sandstones. Limestones in the lower part especially include conglomerates and turbiditic debris beds."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Black mudstones at base of Formation show marked colour change from paler more variegated greys of Worston Shale Group accompanied by conspicuous reduction in bioturbation or where relatively fine-grained limestones of the Pendleside Limestone pass up into coarsely bioclastic limestones of Ravensholme Limestone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H4146 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CR> ;
