        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Thin- to thick-bedded dark grey crinoidal wackestones with abundant chert beds interbedded with mudstones and nodular limestones. Packstones present in uppermost part. Deposited in a distal ramp setting."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at junction of massive dolomitised reef limestones of the Berry Slade Formation and the overlying dark limestones with thin mudstones and cherts of the Formation. Where the top of the Berry Slade Formation is in flank facies, the boundary is imprecise but taken at the increase in chert content at the base of the Linney Head Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H1026 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CI> ;
