    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete] Used in the past to describe Palaeogene deposits beneath the London Clay in the London Basin, especially where the Lambeth Group and the Thanet Formation are difficult to separate, as in Essex, for example. In some places, this may include the Harwich Formation and there would be equivalent to Thanet Formation, Lambeth Group and Harwich Formation (Undifferentiated) [TSLH]."@en ;
