    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Quartzite, flaggy, thin- to thick-bedded, with thin partings of micaceous psammite. Minor semipelite in upper part, in part with calc-silicate lenses."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Fairly sharp change from very thickly-bedded quartzite of Findochty Quartzite Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H4167 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
