    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Reddish brown, green and purple thinly bedded fine-and medium- grained sandstone with a few small silty mudstone clasts in some beds. Local green and grey mottled siltstones and mudstones and conglomerate beds including quartzite pebbles."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base of the predominantly sandstone succession on the southern side of the Eastfield Inlier, faulted against the Lanark Group (Siluro-Devonian)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H388 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SW> ;
