    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The dominant lithology is a creamy micrite in beds up to 0.3 m thick; large ammonites common, interbedded with thick (up to 10 m) calcareous mudstones"@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary is taken at the base of the first significant limestone above the Saltford Shale."@en ;
