    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Quartzose banded gneisses, locally magnetite-rich. Orthopyroxene recorded in parts. Garnets common. Rare semi-pelitic and calc-silicate bands. Geochemically distinct - depleted in K, Rb, Cs, Th, La, B."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "East boundary - fault. Small fault also approximately coincides with west boundary. Generally grades rapidly into highly migmatitic psammites and semi-pelites."@en ;
