    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sand and gravel and red and purple stony clay diamicton (till) with distinctive igneous clasts of western provenance (Bowen p. 147 in Lewis and Richards, 2005). Erratic boulders include tuff (at Pentre), quartz felsite (at Newton and St Athan)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Unconformable contact with bedrock of Silurian to Carboniferous age"@en ;
