    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """See RBDU Raised beach deposits. Raised beach deposits, 1 is older than Raised beach deposits in the same map area. \r
\r
Shingle, sand, silt and clay; may be bedded or chaotic; beach deposits may be in the form of dunes, sheets or banks - [generic description}; now above the level of the present shoreline as a result of earth movement or a general fall in sea level. [Generic description: earth science dictionaries in the BGS library]."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H3642 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
