        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Moderate brown sandy silty gravelly diamicton, very compact, matrix-supported, generally massive, containing moderately well dispersed, subangular to subrounded clasts of granophyre, granite, Borrowdale Volcanic Group rocks (rhyolite, welded tuff, slate), with some red sandstone, ironstone and shell fragments."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Not seen in sections, but probably mainly a sharp, irregular, unconformable contact with bedrock. Locally a sharp, unconformable contact with a sequence of reddish or yellowish brown sand, silt and clay of the Barn Scar Sand and Silt Member of the Seascale Glacigenic Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H2079 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.16e-01 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "To 10m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Sharp, undulating, unconformable contact with overlying sand and gravel deposits or till units of the Gosforth Glacigenic Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.18e-02 ;
