        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Yellowish red sand or sandy gravel with sporadic cobbles. Gravel and cobbles are dominated by well-rounded Sherwood Sandstone derived quartzite but with some rounded erratics of granite, felsite and Coal Measures sandstone. Fossiliferous in part."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Sharp, erosive, unconformable contact with bedrock. Strongly channelised."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H1809 ;
