    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Grey, weathering pale brown, silty, finely sandy, shelly limestone in one or two closely-spaced 0.1 to 0.35 m-thick beds. Upper part may include fine ferruginous peloids. Fauna includes forams, serpulids, gastropods, bivalves (including numerous pectiniids and Gryphaea), ammonites, belemnites, ostracods, fish debris and palynomorphs. Forms a weak feature."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Change up from grey shelly mudstone of the undifferentiated Foston Member; at 10.91 m depth in type section Fulbeck Airfield Borehole F/B5 (SK95SW/17)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H4877 ;
