namedrockunit:SPBA
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BA"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Spout of Ballochleam Lava Member consists predominantly of plagioclase-microphyric basalt lavas (of 'Jedburgh' type) with, near the base, rare olivine-microphyric basalt lavas (of 'Dalmeny' type) [NS 7061 9266], and higher within the member, isolated plagioclase-macrophyric basalt lavas (of 'Markle' type). Many of the basalt lavas are relatively coarse-grained and massive, with no clear distinction between the feldspar phenocrysts and the feldspars in the groundmass. The lavas are also variably, slaggy, vesiculose with amygdales, platy and occasionally columnar jointed, and spheroidally weathered. Dark red-weathered horizons ('boles'), some with nodules of decomposed lava are developed on the tops of some lavas."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "In the northern Touch Hills and the north-eastern Gargunnnock Hills, the basal plagioclase- or olivine-microphyric basalt lava of the member lies unconformably on the eroded plagioclase-macrophyric lavas of the Baston Burn Lava Member, progressively overstepping them to the west. In the north-western Gargunnock Hills and the Fintry Hills, the member overlies conformably or disconformably, tuffs of the Slackgun Volcaniclastic Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H1196 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.445e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "24 to 91 m. The member is of variable thickness, but generally thickens to the west."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "In the north and west Fintry Hills, the member is overlain, apparently conformably or disconformably, by the Shelloch Burn Lava Member and the lithological change is to trachybasalt lava. In the northern Gargunnock Hills and north-western Touch Hills, however, the member is overlain, possibly disconformably, by trachybasalt lava of the Lees Hill Lava Member and in the north-eastern Touch Hills, possibly disconformably, by the Gargunnock Hills Lava Member. In the latter case, the lithogical change is to plagioclase-macrophyric basalt lava."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CR> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.309e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel "Spout of Ballochleam Group [Obsolete: use SPBA]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:CPV ;
    skos:definition "Basalt. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Arundian Substage - to - Asbian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (344.5-330.9 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "SPBA"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Spout of Ballochleam Lava Member"@en ;
.

