namedrockunit:STMH
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Interbedded greenish or greyish brown glauconitic silt, some sandy, and silty clay. \r
\r
The Stourmouth Silt is early to mid-Thanetian in age (NP6 to NP8), based on microfossils (especially nannofossils) (King, in prep.) and magnetostratigraphy (Ali and Jolley, 1996)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base of the Stourmouth Silt Member is taken at the upwards disappearance of the fine-grained sands of the Base Bed Member (BSBD)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H5094 ;
