    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "c. 2000-3000 m (estimate: the unit is nowhere exposed in one single section)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Conformably overlain by Cailleach Head Formation (TCC). The lower contact is only exposed on Gruinard Island - not re-analysed since the Second World War due to anthrax contamination."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AT> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 7.2e+02 ;
