    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Dark blue well-packed sandstone (Bed 13), overlain by harder brown sandstone (Bed 14) with seams of phosphatic nodules near the base and top of the member. Both contain a single discontinuous seam of large, fossiliferous \"doggers\"."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Boundary placed at the upward conformable change from dark blue argillaceous sandstone of Simpson (1985) Bed 12 of the Lower Lobster Member into the dark blue well-packed sandstone of Simpson (1985) Bed 13 of The Crackers Member. This boundary is gradational."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H2478 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KP> ;
