    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Yellow-weathering silty very fine-grained sands, locally bioturbated and with hummocky cross-bedding. Impersistent 0.3m limestone in middle. At base 'Blue Band' - 1.8m of blue-grey mudstone - overlies Margaritatus Stone. At top 2.3m of grey mudstone occurs between the Thorncombiensis Bed and the Beacon Limestone Formation"@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Top of the Margaritatus Stone."@en ;
