        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Tidal river or creek deposits consist of sediments comprising a range of grain sizes from mud to sand, deposited within channels in tidal flats and lagoons. Synonym: tidal channel deposits. \r
\r
Variable lithology. Mainly silt and clay; locally may contain peat, sand and gravel."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:TCHD ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
