    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sand and flint gravel believed by Penning and Jukes-Browne (1881) to have been deposited in a lake or wide reach of river in which there had been Gault islands separated by deeper channels made by the stream as it changed its course from time to time."@en ;
