    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Grey mudstone, sandstone, seatearth and coal.  In the upper part of the member there are several thin Spirorbis limestone beds and the secondary reddening of the succession."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "In the type section, dark grey, carbonaceous mudstone with basal coal of the Burford Coal Member, overlies conformably grey to red mudstone-dominated succession of the Crawley Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H2636 ,
        namedrockunit:H79 ;
