    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Red bedded chert, associated with pillow lava."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The exact base of the Member is not clearly defined, as the cherts may be interbedded or overlie the lavas. An analogous situation is seen in the Marchburn Formation in the Northern Belt of the Southern Uplands, where lavas and cherts are interbedded with each other, and the cherts are similarly identified as late Llandeilo to early Caradoc, based on conodont evidence."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
