        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sand, silty sand and silt, rhythmically bedded, pale yellowish brown, capped by sand and gravel. Individual beds are generally graded sand/silt couplets, 0.2 to 0.4m thick, with planar or ripple-drift cross lamination. The beds are stacked into packages and are probably glaciomarine cyclopsams."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Not observed but probably conformable on the Finglack Till Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:GSG ,
        namedrockunit:H1392 ;
