        "Harrath Tuffs and Lavas [Obsolete: use BWT, HHT]"@en ,
        "The Upper Tuffs [Obsolete: use BWT]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:WB ;
    skos:definition "Rhyolitic tuff. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Caradoc Series (Ordovician Period) (458.2-449.75 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "BWT"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Beck Wood Tuff Member"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:BWYP
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/A> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/PELGN"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/PSMGN"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SPELGN"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Coarse pelitic gneiss, garnetiferous, locally migmatitic, with gneissose semipelite and psammite. Quartzite occurs locally.  Calcsilicate bands are common within psammite."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Overlies conformably the Reidh Psammite Fm (REP); where predominantly siliceous psammitic lithologies pass into predominantly pelitic lithologies."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H4508 ,
        namedrockunit:H4509 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AT> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1e+03 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AT> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Highly variable, possibly up to 2-3 km."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Overlain by the Tarvie Psammite Formation (TAPS) - Loch Eil Group, where predominantly pelitic lithologies pass eastwards into predominantly psammitic lithologies."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AT> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 7.2e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Ben Wyvis Pelite [Obsolete: use BWYP]"@en ,
        "Ben Wyvis Pelitic Schist [Obsolete: use BWYP]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:GLEN ;
    skos:definition "Gneissose pelite, gneissose psammite and gneissose semipelite. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Tonian Period (Precambrian) (1000-720 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "BWYP"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ben Wyvis Pelite Formation"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:BYD
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasLateralEquivalent namedrockunit:TFD ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/P"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Barroway Drove Beds comprise soft grey clays and silty clays which were deposited in salt marshes and shallow water brackish lagoons cut by a complex network of tidal channels and creeks, subsequently infilled with silts and fine grained sands. Rhizomes of the salt-tolerant reed Phragmites occur throughout the clays and thin mats of rotted, drifted stems of reeds and sedges are common at many levels. At outcrop the silts and fine-grained sands that infill the creeks form low sinuous ridges or 'roddons'."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The Barroway Drove Beds rest with unconformity commonly on the Fen Lower Peat but also on the intertidal sands. They also rest unconformably on glaciofluvial sand and gravel and on bedrock."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H1408 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QH> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.18e-02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QH> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/U> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to about 12 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The Barroway Drove Beds are generally overlain by the Nordelph Peat Member or the Terrington Beds. Where the Nordelph Peat is present the upper boundary is obvious, but where the peat is absent and the lithology very similar to the overlying Terrington Beds then the upper boundary is difficult to distinguish. The presence of rootlet remains is characteristic of theTerrington Beds and so may help identify the upper boundary of the Barroway Drove Beds."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QH> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 0e+00 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Fen Clay (Godwin, 1940); Butery Clay (Skertchly, 1877) [Obsolete: use BYD]"@en ,
        "Tidal flat deposits"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:FEND ;
    skos:definition "Clay, sand and silt with subsidiary peat. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Holocene Epoch (Quaternary Period) (.0118-0 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "BYD"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Barroway Drove Beds"@en ;
.

