    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Mudstone, silty, reddish brown with common veins of satin spar gypsum and indurated beds of reddish brown or greenish grey siltstone and very fine-grained sandstone, dolomitic."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Conformable, at gradational upward passage from reddish-brown mudstone of the underlying Sidmouth Mudstone Formation (undivided) to the more strongly indurated, silty gypsiferous mudstone of the Clarborough Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1438 ,
        namedrockunit:H3305 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/TD> ;
