    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "3 to 12 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Conformable, at gradational upward passage from the more strongly indurated, silty gypsiferous mudstone of the Clarborough Member to the reddish-brown mudstone of the overlying Sidmouth Mudstone Formation (undivided)"@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/TD> ;
