namedrockunit:COFD
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/C> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/COAL"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/FEST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LAREN"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Predominantly a thick-bedded, coarse-grained sandstone of 'Pennant'-type (lithic arenite), with subordinate interbeds of grey and green mudstone with ironstone concretions and coal. The sandstone is trough cross-bedded to planar bedded and beds commonly show erosive scours. Sandstone beds from beneath the Coleford High Delf seam are typically fine- to medium-grained. Coal seams up to 1.5 m thick are present within the succession. \r
\r
Fluvial channel deposits. The northward thinning of the member results from the northward progradation of the Pennant Sandstone Formation strata onto barren red measures of the Trenchard Formation. Palaeocurrents and the litharenite petrography of the sandstones of the Coleford Member established that they were derived from the south, as opposed to the northerly source of Trenchard Formation siliciclastic stata (Jones, 1972). \r
\r
The roof of the Coleford High Delf contains non-marine bivalves indicative of the Anthraconauta tenuis Zone (Calver, in Welch and Trotter, 1961) and the plant macrofossil Lobatopteris vestita of the Dicksonites plueckenetii Subzone (Wagner and Spinner, 1972), indicative of a late Asturian age (Cleal and Thomas, 1996)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at the base of the lowermost sandstone of 'Pennant'-type (lithic arenite) of the Coleford Member. Occurs conformably above coarse-grained sandstone of the Trenchard Formation in the north of the Forest of Dean Coalfield and unconformably upon limestone and sandstone of the Pembroke Limestone Group in the south."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H2106 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CAS> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.1e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CAS> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "The formation ranges in thickness from 180 m in the north to 300 m in the south, at the type locality."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Taken at the base of the Brazilly Coal, present at the base of a grey mudstone- dominated succession of the Cinderford Member of the Grovesend Formation. The coal rests conformably upon thick-bedded, coarse-grained sandstone of the Coleford Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CAS> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.075e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel "Coleford Formation [Obsolete: use COFD]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:PES ;
    skos:definition "Lithic-arenite with subsidiary mudstone and trace coal and ironstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Asturian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (310-307.5 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:narrower namedrockunit:CHDC ;
    skos:notation "COFD"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Coleford Member"@en ;
.

