        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SPELGN"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Thin-bedded flaggy calc-silicate, calcareous semipelite and impure metacarbonate rock, with beds of metalimestone; bands of distinctive schistose garnet-muscovite-biotite semipelite in upper part. Calcareous psammite beds sparse but more abundant near top."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Base of lowest limestone bed in sequence of flaggy semipelites and psammites of Cairnfield Calcareous Flag Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H2118 ,
        namedrockunit:H3333 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1e+03 ;
