        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEMPEL"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Quartzite, white to grey, fine-grained. The upper half of the formation is especially pure and glassy, with little feldspar or mica. Includes Tempar Dolomitic Member and some beds of conglomerate."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Sharp change from diamictite of Boulder Bed to fine-grained well-bedded quartzite. However, a 10-20m bed of reworked granite diamictite occurs near the base of the Schiehallion Quartzite Formation on Cnocnan Aighean [NN 7292 5551]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H849 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
