        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/VLSS"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Volcaniclastic siltstone, sandstone, conglomerate and breccia in a bedded succession; intercalated subordinate units of tuff, eutaxitic lapilli-tuff and accretionary lapilli-tuff. Intruded by many peperitic andesite sills."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at the base of the lowest bedded volcaniclastic rock within the sequence of volcaniclastic sedimentary rocks and associated andesite sills, resting on andesite or, locally, dacite within the Birker Fell Andesite Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H224 ,
        namedrockunit:H2775 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/O4> ;
