    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Mudstone siltstone and silty mudstone, forming two fining upwards cycles, with scattered ferruginous ooids, thin siderite mudstone beds, layers of sideritic concretions and layers of phosphate nodules"@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Conformable: sharp change up from dark grey mudstone (Peak Mudstone Member)into muddy siltstone, taken at base of semi-continuous sideritic mudstone bed (Bed 57 of Dean, 1954)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
