    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Tuff and localised basalt lavas, with interbedded mudstone, sandstone and thin limestone. These volcanic beds are distinguished by the presence of tuffaceous sedimentary rocks, mainly sandstones with varying proportions of volcanic debris."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "A conformable boundary upon sedimentary rocks, mainly sandstone, of the Fell Sandstone Formation. Volcanic debris is absent in the underlying sandstones of the Fell Sandstone Formation."@en ;
