        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Grey stony sandy clay diamicton with clasts of Lake District volcanoclistic rocks and Carboniferous Limestone. Contains rip-up clasts of underlying Gillcambon Till at Type Section. Elsewhere in Edenside the unit contains relatively more Permo-Triassic red sandstone and Carboniferous sandstones."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Planar or uneven unconformable boundary with red diamicton of the Gillcambon Till Formation below, or unconformable on bedrock."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H1581 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
