namedrockunit:HAC
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use UPR] \r
\r
The Hales Clay Member comprises clay and silt with variable amounts of sand, and sporadic bentonitic volcanic ash layers. The lower part (HC1) comprises bioturbated silt, whereas the much thicker upper part (HC2) comprises silty clay, silt and sandy silt with thin beds of fine-grained sand. The base of Unit HC2 is an interburrowed omission surface overlain by a glauconitic interval. \r
\r
The genetic interpretation is a marine shelf deposit. \r
\r
Early Eocene (early Ypresian)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Originally, the base of the Hales Clay Member was placed at the base of Unit HC1 where clay and silt overlie glauconitic mudstone of the Ormesby Clay Member (Knox et al., 1990). As emended by Jolley (1996), it was placed at the base of unit HC2, at an interburrowed omission surface overlain by a glauconitic interval (King, in prep.), overlying bioturbated silt of unit HC1, now assigned to the Upnor Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H4106 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GY> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 5.6e+01 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GY> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "About 13 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top of the Hales Clay Member is taken where silty clays, clayey silts and thin sands, give way to the tuffaceous siltstones of the Wrabness Member at a sharply-defined discontinuity surface and with a concentration of glauconite in the overlying sediments (Jolley, 1996)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GY> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.81e+01 ;
    lexicon:isObsoleteEquivalentOf
        namedrockunit:ORW ,
        namedrockunit:UPR ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Hales Clay [Obsolete: use HAC]"@en ,
        "Orwell Member"@en ,
        "Upnor Formation"@en ;
    skos:definition "Obsolete name. Clay and silt. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Ypresian Age (Palaeogene Period) (56-48.1 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "HAC"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hales Clay Member [Obsolete: use ORW, UPR]"@en ;
.

