    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Lower Unit: very coarse cobble-boulder conglomerate, interbedded with, and grading upwards a pebble conglomerate. Followed by a pink to grey coarse, arkosic sandstone, interbedded with thin mudstone. Upper Unit: interbedded fine-grained grey sandstone and thin dark mudstone beds with ripple laminations."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Unconformable upon Lewisian Gneiss inlier (L); unconformity locally sheared."@en ;
