    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sandstone, pale orange-brown, coarse- to very coarse-grained, very thick-bedded; typically low-angle tabular planar-bedded; feeble parallel laminations; sporadic trough cross-stratification. Note: Nottage Crag Grit is a very prominent feature-forming delta top sandstone within a siltstone/fine-grained sandstone interbedded, slumped delta slope formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Sharp base to the coarse-grained sandstone of the Nottage Crag Grit overlying siltstones with fine-grained sandstone beds of the Claughton Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CG> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.27e+02 ;
