    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Wackestones, floatstones and subordinate packstones, fine- to coarse-grained, cherty, muddy, dark-grey, thin- to thick-bedded, commonly with diffuse bed boundaries, interbedded with thin mudstones. Slumping is common."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Not seen at type locality. Upward passage of underlying laminated calcisiltites and mudstones of the Hodder Mudstone Formation (undifferentiated) into wackestones and floatstones of the Raingill Limestone Member."@en ;
