    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Stourbridge: Sand and pebbly sand with gravel lenses. \r
\r
Fluvial: possibly deposited by the proto-Stour River in Stourbridge. \r
\r
Assigned to Oxygen Isotope Stage 5e. The Stourbridge locality includes varied fauna of mammalian bone fragments including hippopotamus, mammoth and woolly rhinoceros (Boulton, 1917), which may in part be reworked."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Stourbridge: Erosive base on bedrock (Sherwood Sandstone Group)."@en ;
