        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Mainly dark brown, laminated organic silt and clay containing fragments of bone, antler and plant debris, with lenses of pebbly sand, pale and dark brown silt, black silty clay and about 30cm of pale grey to white clay at the base. Containing a rich fauna and flora of Middle Devensian age, including bone of woolly rhinoceros and reindeer. Radiocarbon dates on antler fragments range between 33.5 and 29.0 ka BP."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Sharp, conformable contact with sand and gravel of the Armsheugh Sand and Gravel Formation at 10.82m above OD."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H3042 ;
