namedrockunit:TEGR
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Gravel, rounded to sub-angular up to 10cm, and fine- to coarse-grained sand; gravel recorded as composed of vein quartz, quartzite and other metamorphic rocks, Lower Devonian lavas, and dolerite."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Markedly erosive base cut into the Errol Clay Formation and the Culfargie Sand Member of the Forth Clay Formation. This supposedly fluvial unit is usually found in a deep channel cut into pre-existing deposits but is recognized on the flanks too."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1224 ,
        namedrockunit:H2480 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.16e-01 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Veneer on the flanks of channels and up to 25m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Overlain unconformably by the transgressive estuarine sand, silt and clay of the Carey Silt Member (Carse Clay Formation) and also by younger units including the sub-Carse Peat (Flanders Moss Peat Formation) and Carse of Cowrie Clay Member (Carse Clay Formation); also exposed at the surface locally."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.18e-02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Earn Gravel [Obsolete: use TEGR]"@en ,
        "Friarton Gravel [Obsolete: use TEGR]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:FOCL ;
    skos:definition "Gravel and sand with subsidiary silt and trace clay. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Devensian Stage (Quaternary Period) (.116-.0118 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "TEGR"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Tay-Earn Gravels Member"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:TELND
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasLateralEquivalent namedrockunit:S597 ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/P"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Teindland Palaeosol Formation is developed on the surface of the Orbliston Sand Bed and is podzolic in character. It comprises a thin redeposited humic 'H' horizon, a bleached 'Ea' horizon up to 15 cm thick, an intermittently developed iron pan and a lower 'strong brown' (7.5 YR 5/8) 'Bs' horizon, 5 to 15 cm thick. Overlying the humic horizon are thin layers of organic sand with charcoal fragments. At Teindland Quarry, the Badentinan Sand Bed, up to 1.5 m thick, overlies these organic sands. The lower 80-100 cm comprises parallel thin beds of brown polleniferous sand. This pollen was partly derived from reworking of soils around the site and partly from contemporaneous sparse grassland. The upper 50-70 cm of the sand is non-polleniferous. The presence of small gravel clusters, silt balls, an isoclinical fold and of shear zones suggest a glacial or glacitectonic influence on, or more likely following, deposition in a small pond. The Teindland Palaeosol Formation is less well developed at Red Burn, where the parent material is a greenish grey (5 GY 6/1) sandy diamicton and where the overlying organic sediments are thin and disturbed by cryoturbation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "At Teindland Quarry, the Teindland Palaeosol Formation rests unconformably on up to 3 m of very pale brown (10 YR 7/4) sand (Orbliston Sand Bed of the Deanshillock Gravel Formation). At the Red Burn site, the Teindland Palaeosol Formation rests unconformably on a unit of sand with sporadic clasts that appears to correlate with the Deanshillock Gravel Formation at the base of the known sequence at Teindland Quarry."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H4922 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QI> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.26e-01 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QI> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 4 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "At Teindland Quarry the organic sediments of the Teindland Palaeosol Formation are overlain by up to 2.2 m of bedded sandy diamicton, the Woodside Diamicton Formation with crude parallel bedding and localised wash horizons."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QI> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.16e-01 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Teindland Buried Soil [Obsolete: use TELND]"@en ,
        "Teindland Palaeosol Bed [Obsolete: use TELND]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:BCAT ;
    skos:definition "Sand with subsidiary peat and trace silt. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Ipswichian Stage (Quaternary Period) (.126-.116 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "TELND"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Teindland Palaeosol Formation"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:TELPP
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/COAL"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CONG"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/QAREN"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEATM"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Fluvial, fine- to coarse-grained, locally pebbly and conglomeratic, pale grey, quartzitic sandstones with thin argillaceous mudstone/siltstone and seatearth interbeds; sporadic, thin coals in the argillaceous beds."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base is placed at the base of the lowermost quartzitic sandstone of the formation, where it overlies a sharp surface or erosion surface cut in the underlying mudstones of the Bishopston Mudstone Formation. At the type section at Telpyn Point, the boundary is placed at the base of a fine-grained quartzitic sandstone at 27.66m (90' 9\") below the top of the section measured by Archer (1965)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:FR ,
        namedrockunit:H1226 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CK> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.22e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "18.97m at type section to 21.3m at Settling Nose."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top is placed at the top of the highest quartzitic sandstone of the Formation, immediately or close below the base of the dark grey fossiliferous mudstones of the Subcrenatum Marine Band. Note that, for practical mapping purposes, any development of thin non-marine beds between the top of the highest quartzite and the base of the Subcrenatum Marine Band are included in the Telpyn Sandstone Formation. There are 8.7m of these at Telpyn Point and 7.62m at Settling Nose."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CY> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.19e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Farewell Rock [Obsolete: use TELPP]"@en ,
        "Upper Sandstone Group [Obsolete: use TELPP]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:MARR ;
    skos:definition "Quartz-arenite with subsidiary mudstone, seat-earth mudstone and siltstone and trace coal and conglomerate. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Kinderscoutian Substage - to - Yeadonian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (322-319 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "TELPP"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Telpyn Point Sandstone Formation"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:TEVYT
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLateralEquivalent
        namedrockunit:TEVY ,
        namedrockunit:TGP ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/AGG"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BALAVA"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BATUF"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CHRT"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LMST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLTE"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Tintagel Group comprises grey-black slates with siltstones and carbonate nodules, and limestone; coarse- and fine-grained tuffs also occur with agglomerate and lavas. \r
\r
Teign Valley Group predominantly comprises black commonly pyritic mudstones, siliceous mudstones, bedded cherts and some thin limestones. Shallower water formations comprising greenish mudstones with thin limestones and black mudstones with quartzitic sandstones are confined to north Cornwall. Scattered formations and units of basaltic tuff and lava locally are present on the south crop of the group. \r
\r
This composite unit is represented on the BGS 1:625 000 scale Bedrock Geology UK North and South geological maps (BGS 2007) of the UK and some derived digital products such as the UK3D fence diagram model. See the entries for the constituent units for more information."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "On the north crop in north Devon and west Somerset, the lower boundary is taken at the incoming of black, locally siliceous mudstones of the Teign Valley Group (Doddiscombe Mudstone Formation) above the soft mid to dark grey mudstones with scattered very thin fossiliferous limestones, siltstones and sandstones of the underlying Exmoor Group (Pilton Mudstone Formation). On the south crop in south Devon, the lower boundary is taken at the incoming of black, locally siliceous mudstones of the Teign Valley Group (Combe Mudstone Formation) above the olive green and pale grey mudstones of the Trusham Mudstone Formation. Elsewhere on the south crop the base is thrust out. In the west, around Tintagel, the base is taken at the base of grey-black slates of the Barras Nose Formation where they rest apparently conformably on grey slates of the Yeolmbridge Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CF> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.593e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/U> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "100 to 720 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Due to thrusting along the south crop of the Group, the upper boundary is seen only between Okehampton (SX 59 54) and the Teign Valley (SX 84 84), east Dartmoor, Devon. The top is gradational and taken at the incoming of dark grey mudstones with abundant thin- to medium-bedded turbidite sandstones of the overlying Holsworthy Group (Crackington Formation) above the dark grey mudstones with sparse scattered thin turbidite sandstones of the Teign Valley Group (Dowhills Mudstone Formation). On the north crop of the Group, between the Bideford area (SS 45 27), north Devon, and the Westleigh area (ST 06 17), west Somerset, the base is taken at a similar level. Between Bodmin and Dartmoor the group occurs in tectonic slices and no top is seen. The top here is thought to be an unconformity where the overlying Holsworthy Group (Bealsmill Formation) rests unconformably on rocks of the Teign Valley Group, which had already been deformed by D1."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.43e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Teign Valley Group"@en ,
        "Tintagel Group [Obsolete: use TVF]"@en ;
    skos:definition "Chert and mudstone with subsidiary agglomerate, basalt lava, basaltic tuff, limestone, sandstone and siltstone and trace slate. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Courceyan Substage - to - Arundian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (359.3-343 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:isTopConceptOf lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "TEVYT"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Teign Valley Group and Tintagel Group (Undifferentiated)"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:TFICL
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/DMTN"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
