namedrockunit:THN
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The code was originated for use in describing Quaternary Domains in the Sellafield (Cumbria) area. To avoid potential confusion it should be used only for similar purposes in future. See also THNC and THNX. Note that on the related Quaternary Domains map, this category was described as: \"Thin till on rock (generally <5m)\"."@en ;
