    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Interbedded lithic wackes (with subordinate lithic arenites), siltstones and mudstones. Sandstones are fine-grained to granular with abundant siltstone and mudstone intraclasts. Sedimentary structures are uncommon but include normal grading and sole structures."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Boundary with underlying Bitter Beck Formation is gradational and marked by an increase in the proportion of sandstone and a decrease in the proportion of mudstone in the succession. Base taken at the level where sandstone and siltstone predominate."@en ;
