    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "c.3300m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Upper part comprises pale grey-green silty mudstone with fine-grained sandstone streaks, lenses, thick/thin beds of sandstone and lenticular quartzite beds. Boundary with Bovisand Formation marked by colour change to dark grey above. Above the boundary bioturbation, bioclasts and sandstone beds with load casting and cross lamination are progressively more common."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DP> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.105e+02 ;
