namedrockunit:BATH
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BA"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/TFASR"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/TUF"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/TUFT"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """The sequence comprises: \r
\r
At Salsburgh, Lanarkshire, the Salsburgh Volcanic Formation; \r
\r
In Fife, the Kinghorn Volcanic Formation; \r
\r
In West Lothian, the Bathgate Hills Volcanic Formation. \r
\r
These formations are generally characterised by olivine-microphyric basalts and basanites of Dalmeny and Hillhouse types with some olivine-macrophyric basalts of Craiglockhart and Dunsapie types. Bedded tuffites and tuffaceous sedimentary rocks also occur. However, unlike the petrologically wide ranging volcanic rocks of the Clyde Plateau Volcanic Formation (Strathclyde Group) of the western Midland Valley of Scotland, these formations are not readily subdivided into members. \r
\r
The depositional environment is subaerial to submarine. Asbian to Arnsbergian in age."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base of the group is taken at an upward transition from sedimentary rocks in most areas, but is drawn at the top of the Clyde Plateau Volcanic Formation in the Rashiehill Borehole (BGS Registration Number NS87SW/22) [NS 8386 7301], west of Slammanan, and at a supposed unconformity in the Salsburgh 1A oil well (BGS Registration Number NS86SW/89) [NS 8166 6487]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CR> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.37e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/G> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "It is very variable in thickness, locally in excess of 450 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top is taken at the top of the highest known pyroclastic rock interdigitated in the Passage Formation (Clackmannan Group) (fluviodeltaic ('Millstone Grit') facies) in the Central Coalfield area (see Cameron et al. 1998, p. 50)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CG> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.2375e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:definition "Basalt with subsidiary tuff, tuffaceous-sedimentary-rock and tuffite. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Asbian Substage - to - Arnsbergian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (337-323.75 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
