namedrockunit:BFB
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLateralEquivalent namedrockunit:BRKH ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CALSIR"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/FEST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/HFMDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/HFSDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LMST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use ADS, BRKH] \r
\r
The Broadford Beds Formation is fully described by Morton and Hudson, 1995, though Hesselbo et al, (1998) contradict this and rename the units described. BGS maps are based on the former reference. The description includes BHLS, BRKH and ADS, which are also documented in the Lexicon. The lower Broadford Beds are dominated by carbonate rocks, calcareous mudstones and mature sandstones. Coral-rich beds are abundant in the lowermost parts and are overlain by restricted marine-fauna-rich lagoonal sediments. A shallowing of marine conditions from neritic deposition during Blue Lias times to nearshore/lagoonal is inferred. The upper Broadford Beds comprise sandstones and sandy siltstones. Typically these are highly micaceous and ferriginous. An ironstone bed with chamosite is found on the Ardnish Peninsula. A diverse marine faunal assemblage is common."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Transitional, transgressive mudstones and sandstones from underlying Triassic."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1345 ,
        namedrockunit:H6 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JH> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.014e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "50 to 100m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Abrupt facies change to Pabay Shale Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JS> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.929e+02 ;
    lexicon:isObsoleteEquivalentOf namedrockunit:ADS ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Ardnish Formation"@en ,
        "Breakish Formation"@en ,
        "Lower Broadford Beds [Obsolete: use BFB, BRKH]"@en ,
        "Upper Broadford Beds [Obsolete: use ADS, BFB]"@en ;
    skos:definition "Obsolete name. Sandstone with subsidiary limestone, mudstone and siltstone and trace calcsilicate-rock, hornfelsed mudstone, hornfelsed sandstone and ironstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Hettangian Age - to - Sinemurian Age (Jurassic Period) (201.4-192.9 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "BFB"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Broadford Beds Formation [Obsolete: use ADS, BRKH]"@en ;
.

