        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Mid to dark grey massive mudstones, commonly slumped and destratified, with rafts and balled inclusions of sandstone; local thin-bedded siltstones."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Overlies the Pencerrigtewion Member of the Drosgol Formation (Cave and Hains, 1986), with apparent conformity, although the boundary is likely to represent one or more syndepositional slide planes. Where the Pencerrigtewion Member disappears, the Formation cannot be distinguished from the underlying Drosgol Formation, and both have been grouped as the Garnedd-wen Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1351 ,
