        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/TUFCY"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Thick- to thin-bedded intermediate to mafic crystal tuffs and rare felsic tuffs, interbedded with pillowed lavas, hyaloclastites, and tuffaceous siltstones and mudstones."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Overlies mudstones and siltstones of the Ty'r Gawen Mudstone Formation, though with possible unconformity or non-sequence in places. Northwards from the Cadair Idris district it oversteps the Melau Formation to rest on the Allt Lwyd Formation in the Harlech district."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:S554 ,
        namedrockunit:SER ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/OE> ;
