namedrockunit:BME
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/COAL"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """[Obsolete: use WAWK] \r
\r
Sandstones, siltstones and mudstones, predominantly reddish, brownish or purplish grey coloured but with some grey strata; coal seams not common. BARREN MEASURES: this term is reintroduced to include red-bed formations and relatively coal-poor grey formations overlying Productive Coal Measures in the Midlands. It comprises the Etruria, Newcastle, Keele, Halesowen, Enville and Coventry Sandstone units and the Ardwick units. The earliest definition of similar terms (Barren [Coal] Measures) was by Vernon (1912, p.593) in the Warwickshire Coalfield, as comprising the Nuneaton Clays (Etruria Formation), Haunchwood Sandstones (Newcastle Formation) and Keele Beds (Keele Formation). He excluded overlying red beds with conglomerates that are now included."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Base of lowest red-bed formation above grey Coal Measures; or of late Carboniferous age if Coal Measures absent."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H2624 ,
        namedrockunit:H2625 ,
        namedrockunit:H4477 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CW> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.19e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/G> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 1,192 metres in the Potteries Syncline."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Base of unconformable Permian or younger strata."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CS> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.005e+02 ;
    lexicon:isObsoleteEquivalentOf namedrockunit:WAWK ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/deprecated> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Barren Measures [Obsolete: use BME]"@en ,
        "Coal Measures, Upper (E and W) [Obsolete: use BME]"@en ,
        "Red Barren Coal Measures [Obsolete: use BME]"@en ,
        "Warwickshire Group"@en ;
    skos:definition "Obsolete name. Mudstone, sandstone and siltstone with subsidiary coal. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Westphalian Stage - to - Stephanian Stage (Carboniferous Period) (319-300.5 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "BME"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Barren Measures Group [Obsolete: use WAWK]"@en ;
.

