    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The upper part is a  dominantly laminated reddish-brown and greenish-grey mudstone with siltstones. The lower part is a structureless and laminated, dominantly reddish-brown mudstone. Within the lower part of the member,  a unit termed the 'Lower Keuper Sandstone' has been recognised in the Stockport area. This unit closely resembles the Tarporley Siltstone Formation of adjacent areas."@en ;
