        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLTE"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The Group consists of quartz-arenites and turbiditic sandstones of the Lower Cambrian Brand Hills Formation, which in turn pass up to grey, cleaved mudrocks of the Swithland Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base of the Group is unexposed, but is inferred to be unconformable upon units of Neoproterozoic III age that include intrusive rocks of the South Charnwood Diorites and tuffaceous mudstones, siltstones and sandstones of the Bradgate Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H2054 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/EC> ;
