        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/ZC"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Generically it varies from silt to clay, commonly yellow-brown. Origin uncertain. Commonly includes a high percentage of wind-blown, silt-sized quartz (possibly loess). Locally represented by yellow to buff sand with shells at base passing up through brown, bedded sand with sandy silt to grey clay and shelly sand at the top."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Overlies Interglacial gravel and sand"@en ;
