        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sandstone with interbedded, laminated slaty mudstone and siltstone. The sandstones are predominantly fine- to medium-grained and form thinning- and fining-upwards sequences. Channel fills and slumps are evident in the lower to middle parts of the Formation, while the upper part is characterised by thinly to thickly bedded turbidites."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Conformable above Pendower Formation."@en ;
