Mudstone (claystone) grey to blue-grey, shaly, fossiliferous (bivalves and goniatites) with common calcite mudstone nodules and siderite-mudstone lenses in upper part."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Sharp boundary, with grey to blue-grey mudstone of the Caton Shale Member above fine-grained sandstone of the Ward's Stone Sandstone."@en ;
