        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sandstone (wacke), thin- to medium-bedded with interbedded siltstone and mudstone, locally including laminated carbonaceous siltstone and thin beds of meta-bentonite."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Visible contacts are all faulted against the Manx Group and Peel Formation. It is likely that both lower and upper stratigraphical contacts are unconformable - the lower on the Manx Group where distinguished by being sandstone-dominated facies as opposed to a mudstone, the upper probably with overlying Permian or Triassic red-bed facies."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H3975 ,
        namedrockunit:MXSL ;
