    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "110.97 m is the maximum measured thickness [SD81SW/3], allthough the bottom was not proved."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary is taken at the base of a mudstone-dominated succession overlying sandstones of the Fletcher Bank Grit; often coincident with the base of an unnamed coal."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CZ> ;
