    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Medium to dark grey laminated, micaceous and partly calcareous sandy siltstone containing carbonaceous debris. Near the base calcareous nodules occur in layers.  Includes unit of turbiditic sandstone referred to as the Studfold Sandstone Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at the sharp comformable base of a thick sequence of sandy siltstone overlying thickly bedded calcareous siltstone of the Arcow Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
