    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A pale to dark grey bioclastic (crinoidal) marine limestone, with algal nodules. The name is not geographical in origin, but indicates a marker bed for the Limestone Coal Formation coal seams below."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally a conformable change from a marine mudstone almost at the top of the Limestone Coal Formation. The Index Limestone as it is usually called, forms the base of the Upper Limestone Formation."@en ;
