namedrockunit:LRB
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/C> ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BA"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LMST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/TUF"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Dark green, grey or brown basalt lava with interbedded tuff and locally, in the Masson Hill (SK 286 587) - Bonsall area (SK 2758), interdigitations of limestone and tuffaceous limestone (Chisholm et al., 1983; Walters and Ineson, 1981). At Masson Hill three distinct lava flows are recognized, characterised by vesicular upper and lower surfaces, separated by tuff or decomposed clay (Walters and Ineson, 1981), with the lower two flows containing abundant marmorised limestone and angular basaltic fragments. Typically amygdaloidal towards the top of the lava flows and may include haematite veinlets. Locally, the lavas include vertical wedges of clay representing partial weathering of the basalt (Smith et al., 1967). In places the weathering of the basalt to a grey or brown clay is complete, although the presence of amygdales indicates origin as a lava."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally, the basalt lava of the Lower Matlock Lava Member rests upon thickly bedded limestones of the Monsal Dale Limestone Formation. At Hoptonwoodstone Quarry (SK 277 557) the basal c.3m comprises amygdaloidal basalt, thoroughly altered to grey and yellow clay, with lenses of pink limestone (Smith, 1967). The base of the lava, here, has been interpreted as a palaeokarstic surface with pits up to 10m deep filled by weathered blocks of lava, tuff and limestone in a clay matrix (Walters, 1981). South of Bonsall the formation thins markedly and around Golconda Mine (SK 249 551) a thin lava rests upon pale grey calcarenites of the Bee Low Limestone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1045 ,
        namedrockunit:H1046 ,
        namedrockunit:H375 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CX> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.309e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CX> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Maximum of 99m at Masson Hill (SK 286 587); about 50m thick in boreholes north of Winster."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Lavas and tuffs of the Lower Matlock Lava Member are overlain by thickly bedded limestones of the Monsal Dale Limestone Formation. At Hoptonwoodstone Quarry (SK 277 557) the uppermost 0.3m-thick bed of the Member comprises brecciated limestone in a matrix of clay with vestiges of amygdales (weathered basalt)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CX> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.303e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Lower Matlock Lava [Obsolete: use LRB]"@en ,
        "Matlock Lower Basalt [Obsolete: use LRB]"@en ,
        "Matlock Lower Lava [Obsolete: use LRB]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:MO ;
    skos:definition "Basalt and tuff with subsidiary limestone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Brigantian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (330.9-330.3 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "LRB"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Lower Matlock Lava Member"@en ;
.

