    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """White pure chalk with some flint seams and very shelly beds. Comprises from base: hard indurated chalk with flaser marls (Melbourn Rock) to exceptionally shelly chalk with flints into chalk with well defined marl seams. \r
\r
Name remains in informal use but generally regarded as obsolete onshore."""@en ;
