    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A suite of fluvial, lacustrine, mass movement, periglacial and aeolian deposits that contain clasts derived from rocks cropping out in northeastern England (mainly sandstone, gritstone, mudstone, limestone and coal), including alluvium, river terrace deposits, peat, head and blown sand."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Unconformable contact with units of the North Pennine and North Sea Coast Glacigenic subgroups, and with bedrock."@en ;
