    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Raised tidal flat deposits are isostatically uplifted tidal flat deposits which crop out in part above high water mark. \r
\r
Normally a consolidated soft silty clay, with layers of sand, gravel and peat. Characteristically low relief."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/Q> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.58e+00 ;
