    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition """The lower boundary is conformable (but see comments re thickness). Inferred to be at the Whitecliff Wispy Marls (at Whitecliff Bay) at the boundary between the Sompting and Whitecliff beds of Mortimore (1986). \r
\r
In mapping terms taken just below a marked feature break that is thought to be formed by either a hardground or a thick bed of flints."""@en ;
