    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "30 m at Whitecliff Bay; thought to be as thick as 45 m in Dorset and around 35 m in Hampshire."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary is conformable at the Portsdown Marl 1 in the Farlington Redoubt on Portsdown and at Whitecliff Bay, Isle of Wight."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KC> ;
