    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Talus cone refers to a matrix-supported or matrix-rich, cone-like accumulation of rock fragments of any size or shape at the foot of a gully or chute in a cliff or steep slope. Formed by mass-movement-rainwash, sheetwash, debris flow, mudslide or avalanche."@en ;
