        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Mainly silty clays and clays, some sandy or gravelly, with some silts, sands, gravels and calcareous mudstones. \r
\r
The Thames Group was deposited in environments ranging from marine shoreface ranging out to outer marine shelf. \r
\r
Eocene (early and middle Ypresian)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base of the Thames Group is the base of the Harwich Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H1227 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GY> ;
