    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "To about 60m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Overlain by uniform, bioturbated calcareous siltstone of the Torver Member. The top of the Applethwaite Member is taken as the top of the highest graded unit, which is transitional into the overlying and more homogeneous siltstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/OU> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.4875e+02 ;
