    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Semipelites with subsidiary psammites, generally phyllitic, more calcareous in its upper part. Distinctive white limestone bands typically. Also grey finely crystalline limestones and calc-silicate bands. In Glenlivet-Glen Suie area divided into three members."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "At upper limit of quartzite of the Corryhabbie Quartzite Formation and at lowest occurrence of white limestone or semipelite."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1e+03 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "40 - 600m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Rapid gradation from calcareous semipelite and limestone to graphitic pelite/semipelite of Clashnoir Semipelite Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 5.41e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:DABH ;
    skos:definition "Semipelite with subsidiary calcsilicate-rock, limestone and psammite and trace metalimestone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Neoproterozoic Era (Precambrian) (1000-541 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:narrower
        namedrockunit:ALDP ,
