    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "White, pink and yellow siliceous sands with brightly coloured silts and clays, lying in pockets caused by karstic dissolution of Carboniferous limestones. Divided into: Kirkham Member, Bees' Nest Member and Kenslow Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary is a sharp, unconformable contact on karstified limestones which form hollows, or 'pockets', for the formation."@en ;
