    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete: use PENDL] A medium- to thickly-bedded, brownish grey, medium- to coarse-grained sandstone and pebbly sandstone, which is massive to coarse bedded; beds of siltstone can occur throughout and locally coals are developed. The unit is interpreted as a delta top sandstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "A sharp upward change in a conformable succession from the predominantly grey mudstone to sandstone-base of first pebbly sandstone bed above the Pendle Grit Member."@en ;
