    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Glacigenic deposits are sediments laid down within or under glacier ice or deposited by an ice sheet. \r
\r
Includes many types of sediment (e.g. clay, silt, sand and gravel) dependent on source rock and age and style of ice movement. Heterogeneous deposits often referred to non-genetically as diamicton."""@en ;
