        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Gravel overlain by sand; a high proportion of the gravel includes exotic clasts from Scotland, Lake District and Malvern Hills; third terrace of the River Severn, also known as the 'Main Terrace'; part of the Severn Valley Formation. [Generic description: academic papers and BGS Memoirs]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H3050 ,
        namedrockunit:HHTD ,
        namedrockunit:HOHE ;
