        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SHMDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Olive-grey, silty, calcareous mudstones with thin intervals of argillaceous limestone and oyster-rich mudstones (9 divisions: see principal reference)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "A rapid increase in shell-detritus in calcareous mudstones that pass into the uppermost limestone of the Inferior Oolite."@en ;
