    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Limestone (chalk) with many tabular flint bands and Inoceramus debris in upper part. In the south Antrim area  (Southern Uplands High) there are important hardground non-sequences of green-coated chalk pebbles called the South Antrim Hardgrounds (of ?member status)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary is conformable, on the Garron Chalk Formation, at a bedding plane beneath a prominent continuous tabular flint."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1770 ,
        namedrockunit:H1771 ,
        namedrockunit:H2379 ,
        namedrockunit:H2748 ;
