        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Interbedded grey mudstone, siltstone, pale grey sandstone and commonly coal seams, with a bed of mudstone containing marine fossils at the base, and several such marine fossil-bearing mudstones in the upper half of the unit. \r
\r
This composite unit is represented on the BGS 1:625 000 scale Bedrock Geology UK North and South geological maps (BGS 2007a, b) of the UK and some derived digital products such as the UK3D fence diagram model. See the entries for the constituent units for more information."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base of the dark grey, fissile mudstone of the Vanderbeckei Marine Band, with eponymous fauna and/or other marine fossils (see Stubblefield and Trotter, 1957)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:GRM ,
        namedrockunit:H3064 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CB> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.18e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/U> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 600 m thick across the North Staffordshire Coalfield; about 650 m thick in Lancashire; 200 m thick in northwest England and in the northwest of the Canonbie Coalfield. c.120 m on east crop of the South Wales Coalfield [SO 20] to 240 m in the Swansea area [SS 88]."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top of the dark grey, fissile mudstone of the Cambriense Marine Band, with eponymous fauna and/or other marine fossils (see Stubblefield and Trotter, 1957). This definition is extended to the Scottish Solway area, which formerly used the top of the Aegiranum (Skelton) Marine Band to define the top of the formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CC> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.1e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Grey Measures of Yorkshire and Nottingham [Obsolete: use PLCM, PMCM, PSLCM, PSMCM]"@en ,
        "Middle Coal Measures [Obsolete: use PSMCM, SWMCM]"@en ,
        "Pennine Middle Coal Measures Formation"@en ,
        "South Wales Middle Coal Measures Formation"@en ;
    skos:definition "Mudstone, sandstone and siltstone with subsidiary coal, ironstone and seat-earth mudstone and trace ganister and seat-earth sandstone. Bedrock. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Duckmantian Substage - to - Bolsovian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (318-310 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:isTopConceptOf lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "PSMCM"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pennine Middle Coal Measures Formation and South Wales Middle Coal Measures Formation (Undifferentiated)"@en ;
