namedrockunit:RDEPS
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Residual deposits are the weathering products remaining in situ following alteration of a parent material by the action of chemical and/or physical weathering processes. Includes transitional elements (saprolite) between parent material and soil. Includes clay-dominated deposits (e.g. clay-with-flints), coarse (e.g. blockfield) and poorly-sorted deposits (e.g. regolith)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/G> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 6.6e+01 ;
