    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Diamicton, clayey and sandy, typically reddish brown to pale yellowish brown, boulder-sized clasts mainly of Orcadian Devonian sandstones, conglomerates, siltstones and mudstones where overlying Devonian strata, otherwise mainly of Caledonian igneous and Moine metamorphic rocks (Thormaid Till Member) when overlying or near basement outcrops."@en ;
