        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Mainly comprises sand and gravel, forming river terraces, and silty, clayey sand forming floodplains, and concealing sand and gravel. Includes units of sand, silt and clay, which are typically reddish brown."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "A sharp, undulating, erosional contact, mainly on reddish brown, clayey, sandstone-rich diamictons of the Gretna Till Formation, or yellowish brown, greywacke-rich diamictons of the Langholm Till Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QH> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.18e-02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QH> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "To 15m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "At the present ground surface or, locally, covered by peat."@en ;
