    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "[Obsolete: use SILS] Fine- to very coarse-grained sandstone with thin coals and seatearths.Trough cross-bedding in sets up to 0.5m thick. Planar cross-bedding, small-scale cut-and-fill structures, syndepositional faults and slump structures have been recorded."@en ;
