namedrockunit:SYDR
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/V"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Includes fluvial deposits (alluvium and river terrace deposits) of the entire catchment of the Solway Firth bordering the coast between Stranraer and St Bees Head (McMillan and Hamblin, 2000). \r
\r
A suite of fluvial and associated organic deposits that contain clasts derived from Palaeozoic rocks and glacigenic deposits cropping out in the catchment of the Solway Firth, including the Rivers Cree, Dee (Kirkcudbright), Nith, Annan, Esk, Eden. \r
\r
River terraces and floodplains. \r
\r
Late Devensian to Holocene (MIS 2-1)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally an unconformable boundary with units of the Caledonia Glacigenic Group."@en ;
