namedrockunit:ARDNA
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A component of the Hebridean Province comprising three geographically and petrologically related centres (Ardnamurchan Centre 1 (ARD1), Ardnamurchan Centre 2 (ARD2), and Ardnamurchan Centre 3 (ARD3)) forming the Ardnamurchan peninsula. Includes a wide variety of intrusive and extrusive igneous rocks, together with both sedimentary and metamorphic country rocks, particularly in major vent-complexes."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/G> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 6.6e+01 ;
