    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Slaty mudstone, medium to dark grey, with thin sandstone beds and sporadic thin limestone beds. Packets of quartzitic sandstone beds are present in the form of the Upper and Lower Longsands Sandstone members."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Faulted out; overthrust by the Whitsand Bay Formation. Transitional boundary with Whitsand Bay Formation in the Rame Peninsula; grey slaty mudstone passing down into purple slaty mudstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H76 ,
        namedrockunit:H97 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DP> ;
