    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "From 1.2m to 1.6m in the Eyemouth and north Berwickshire districts."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Generally a conformable change to marine mudstone, which in turn passes up into deltaic arenaceous deposits of the Tyne Limestone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CR> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.309e+02 ;
