    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Brown, red, purple, yellow and cream coloured feldspathic sandstone, commonly containing bands of red siltstone and pebbles of silty mudstone, but no siliceous pebbles."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The boundary is gradational, and is drawn at the base of the brown, yellow, red, purple or cream sandstones of the Glenvale Sandstone Formation, where it rests conformably on the red or purple pebbly sandstones of the Burnside Sandstone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:CHB ,
        namedrockunit:H4673 ;
