    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 350 m thick in the Lomond Hills area."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Drawn at the probable conformable upward passage from brown, yellow, red, purple or cream sandstones of the Glenvale Formation to the white or cream sandstones of the Knox Pulpit Sandstone Formation. In the Cupar area, the Dura Den Member intervenes."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DU> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.593e+02 ;
