    skos:definition "Basalt lava, basaltic tuff and lava with subsidiary sedimentary rock based on grain size or crystal size and volcaniclastic rocks (both pyroclastic and reworked volcanic rocks) and trace limestone, mugearite, olivine-clinopyroxene-macrophyric basaltic-rock, plagioclase-macrophyric basaltic-rock, plagioclase-olivine-clinopyroxene-macrophyric basalt, plagioclase-olivine-clinopyroxene-macrophyric basaltic-rock, trachybasalt and trachytic tuff. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Visean Age (Carboniferous Period) (346.7-330.3 Ma BP)."@en ;
