namedrockunit:RANN
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Northern East Shetland Basin: The formation comprises an upward coarsening succession from mudstone (informally the 'Rannoch Mudstone unit' of Richards et al., 1993) to very fine- or fine-grained sandstone. \r
\r
Southern East Shetland Basin: Upward coarsening sandstones (the 'Rannoch Mudstone unit' is absent). \r
\r
Sandstones are often parallel laminated and hummocky cross-stratified, micaceous, and carbonaceous along the laminations. Individual beds have sharp bases and may show an upward succession from laminated or hummocky cross-stratified sandstone to ripple laminated sandstone. Bioturbation is extensive. Locally calcite-cemented. \r
\r
The 'Ranoch Mudstone unit' comprises a heterolithic succession of interbedded mudstones, siltstones and sandstones.  Mudstones and siltstones are dark grey, carbonaceous, micaceous and laminated. Low angle scours truncate laminations in places. Sandstones are thin, very fine-grained and micaceous. Bioturbation is locally intense. \r
\r
South-western East Shetland Basin: Fine-grained, locally medium-grained sandstone."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition """East Shetland Basin: In the southern part of the East Shetland Basin the boundary is placed at a downward change from very fine-grained, micaceous sandstone to coarser sandstones (Broom Formation). In the northern part of the East Shetland Basin the boundary is marked by a downward change from micaceous mudstones ('Rannoch Mudstone unit') to coarse sandstone (Broom Formation). In both areas there is a down-section decrease in gamma values. \r
\r
South-western part of the East Shetland Basin: downward transition from fine-grained- to medium-grained, micaceous, laminated sandstones (Rannoch Formation) to coarse grained sandstone (Broom Formation). This corresponds to the base of an interval of increased gamma-ray values. \r
\r
North eastern part of East Shetland Basin: micaceous mudstones ('Rannoch Mudstone unit') overlie poorly micaceous mudstones of the Drake Formation (Dunlin Group). This corresponds with a slight down-section decrease in gamma values and increase in velocity."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H5198 ,
        namedrockunit:H5199 ,
        namedrockunit:H5200 ,
        namedrockunit:H5201 ,
        namedrockunit:H5202 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JA> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.747e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to c. 100 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The boundary is defined by a sharp downward change from coarser, less micaceous, generally structureless sandstones (Etive Formation) to finer, micaceous, laminated sandstones. It coincides with a downward increase in gamma values and and often a downward increase in velocity."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JB> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.682e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Micaceous Sand Bed [Obsolete: use RANN]"@en ,
        "Micaceous Sand [Obsolete: use RANN]"@en ,
        "Rannoch Mudstone Unit [Obsolete: use RANN]"@en ,
        "Rannoch Shale [Obsolete: use RANN]"@en ,
        "Rannoch Sub-Unit [Obsolete: use RANN]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:BRNT ;
    skos:definition "Sandstone with subsidiary mudstone and siltstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs offshore. Deposited during the Aalenian Age - to - Bajocian Age (Jurassic Period) (174.7-168.2 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "RANN"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rannoch Formation"@en ;
.

