        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """See RMD Raised marine and coastal zone deposits. \r
\r
Variable lithology. Gravel (shingle), sand, silt and clay; commonly charged with organic debris (plant and shell); now above the level of the present shoreline as a result of earth movement or a general fall in sea level; of Flandrian age. [Generic description: from East Anglian data]."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H5256 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QH> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.18e-02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QH> ;
