    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Floodplain alluvium comprises soft silts and clays, commonly with beds of peat and a basal bed of sand and gravel. River terrace deposits are largely sand and gravel. Peat is a minor component, and minor marine deposits are included where they are intercalated in dominantly fluvial formations."@en ;
