namedrockunit:STRM
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/J> ;
    lexicon:hasLateralEquivalent namedrockunit:PIPR ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/COAL"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """The Stroma Member comprises predominantly interbedded sandstones, carbonaceous silty mudstones and coals.  Sandstones are subarkosic (Maher and Harker, 1987). Reworked volcaniclastics are locally present east of the Piper Field (e.g. North Sea Blocks 15/17 and 15/18). Six lithofacies have been described (Harker et al., 1993): \r
\r
1. Laminated silty mudstones with a thin, poorly sorted, basal lag sandstone. \r
\r
2. Thinly interbedded sandstones and silty mudstones with abundant plant remains. \r
\r
3. Fine-grained, ripple and planar bedded sandstones. \r
\r
4. Upward-coarsening, cross-bedded and massive sandstones. \r
\r
5. Upward fining, cross-bedded sandstones with gravel lag bases and common plant rootlets in the upper part. \r
\r
6. Silty coals grading to carbonaceous silty mudstones. \r
\r
In the Claymore area these facies are arranged in upward coarsening cycles, 3-10 m in thickness."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The boundary is variable. In Block 15/21 (in the type section) the boundary is defined by a downward change from mudstone to tuffs and lava flows (Rattray Volcanic Member). Elsewhere in the Witch Ground Graben, coals sandstones and mudstones (Stroma Member) rest on tuffaceous mudstones and sandstones (Pentland Formation), grey-green and brown mudstones and siltstones (Skagerrak Formation) or red-brown mudstones (Smith Bank Formation). Where the Stroma Member overlies paralic sediments of the Pentland Formation, the boundary cannot be defined with certainty. In the South Halibut Basin, interbedded sandstones, mudstones and coals (Stroma Member) rest on sandstones (Lossiehead Formation), reddish brown and grey Triassic mudstones (Smiths Bank Formation) or, locally, Permian carbonates and evaporites."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H5143 ,
        namedrockunit:H5145 ,
        namedrockunit:H5146 ,
        namedrockunit:H5147 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JO> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.615e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JO> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/M> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to c. 40 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "In the type section and in the South Halibut Basin, the top is defined by a sharp, down-section transition from silty mudstones (Heather Formation) to coal. There is a sharp down-section decrease in gamma ray values, a decrease in velocity and an increase in resistivity. In the Witch Ground Graben, the top of the member is marked by a down-section transistion from mudstones (Heather Formation) to interbedded sandstones, mudstones and coal, accompanied by a downward decrease in gamma-ray values. Locally thin, glauconitic, marine sandstones (Pibroch Member, Piper Formation) rest on carbonaceous sandstones (Stroma Member)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JO> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.548e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Coal Marker Member [Obsolete: use STRM]"@en ,
        "Coal Unit [Obsolete: use STRM]"@en ,
        "Paralic Unit [Obsolete: use STRM]"@en ,
        "Piper Formation"@en ,
        "Skene Member [Obsolete: use GORS, STRM]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:PNTL ;
    skos:definition "Coal, mudstone and sandstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs offshore. Deposited during the Oxfordian Age (Jurassic Period) (161.5-154.8 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "STRM"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Stroma Member"@en ;
.

