    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top is taken at the base of the Pennant Sandstone Formation (Warwickshire Group), where grey, productive coal-bearing mudrocks of the South Wales Coal Measures Group are overlain conformably either by the first substantial development of Pennant sandstones or by red beds of the Deri Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CC> ;
