    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Quartzite and quartz arenite with a thin basal conglomerate. the name Basal Quartzite Member is more accurate and up-to-date than the existing name of False-Bedded Quartzite Member, which is a term no longer used by many experts in this sequence, or in most recent literature. The latter name is also geologically misleading, although it does have a long history of use."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Defined where a thin conglomerate at the base of the Basal Quartzite Member lies above an angular unconformity and oversteps both the Lewisian Complex and the Torridon Group."@en ;
