    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Generally about 0.5 to 0.6m but up to 1.4m in the Cleveland Basin."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary is conformable at the junction between a sticky green clay (Bed 6 i.e. the top of the \"Variegated beds\", in Figure 4, Wood and Mortimore, 1995) and an extremely condensed succession of shell-detrital limestones with some thin very dark \"marl\" seams."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KT> ;
