    skos:definition "Trace agglomerate, albitised felsite, andesite, andesitic-rock, aplitic microgranite, appenitic dioritic-rock, appinitic diorite, basalt, basaltic-andesite, basaltic-rock, biotite granite, biotite-feldspar porphyry, breccia, brecciated-feldspar-quartz pegmatite, dacite, diorite, dioritic-rock, dolerite, feldspar-phyric microdiorite, feldspar-porphyry, felsite, foliated felsite, foliated gabbro, foliated granite, foliated melamicrodiorite, foliated microdiorite, foliated microgranite, foliated quartz-microdiorite, foliated-feldspar-phyric microgranodiorite, foliated-feldspar-quartz pegmatite, foliated-hornfelsed microdiorite, foliated-hornfelsed-porphyritic microdiorite, foliated-porphyritic felsite, foliated-porphyritic microdiorite, gabbroic-rock, gneissose granite, granite, granodiorite, granophyric microgranite, hornblende diorite, hornblende meladiorite, hornblende-phyric microdiorite, hypersthene andesite, intrusion-breccia, kersantite, lamprophyre, leucogranite, leucomicrodiorite, melamicrodiorite, microdiorite, microdioritic-rock, microgabbroic-rock, microgranite, microgranodiorite, micromonzodiorite, microtonalite, minette, monzodiorite, monzonite, olivine monzonite, pegmatite, pegmatitic granite, porphyritic andesite, porphyritic felsite, porphyritic microdiorite, porphyritic microgranite, porphyritic microgranodiorite, porphyry, pyroxene-bearing microdiorite, pyroxene-mica diorite, quartz (vein), quartz-diorite, quartz-feldspar-porphyry, quartz-leucomicrodiorite, quartz-leucomicromonzodiorite, quartz-melamicrodiorite, quartz-melamicromonzodiorite, quartz-microdiorite, quartz-microgabbro, quartz-micromonzodiorite, quartz-monzodiorite, quartz-phyric felsite, quartz-porphyry, rhyolite, rhyolitic pyroclastic-rock, riebeckite felsite, serpentinite, sheared felsite, sheared microdiorite, sheared microgranodiorite, spessartite, tonalite, trachyandesite, tuffisite, ultramafic-rock, vogesite and volcaniclastic-breccia. Igneous intrusive bedrock. Occurs onshore. Emplaced during the Silurian Period - to - Devonian Period (443.1-359.3 Ma BP)."@en ;
