        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sequence of predominantly mudstone, siltstone and sandstone, with common shelly fauna at many levels, variously calcareous, carbonaceous, bituminous, with thin sandy limestone beds, ironstone beds, thin coal seams, a basal conglomerate and boulder beds towards the top."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Unconformity: nodular carbonate rock of the Stotfield Cherty Rock Formation (Triassic) overlain by interbedded conglomerate and sandstone of the Dunrobin Pier Conglomerate Member of the Dunrobin Bay Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JH> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 2.014e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/G> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "At least 1400m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Top of the interbedded boulder beds, sandstone and mudstone beds of the Helmsdale Boulder Beds Formation, not at outcrop onshore. Overlying bedrock formation is unknown."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JI> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.431e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:definition "Bituminous mudstone, mudstone, sandstone and siltstone with subsidiary conglomerate, ferruginous sandstone and glauconitic sandstone and trace coal, ironstone and limestone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Hettangian Age - to - Tithonian Age (Jurassic Period) (201.4-143.1 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:isTopConceptOf lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:narrower
        namedrockunit:BALR ,
        namedrockunit:BOCO ,
        namedrockunit:CYK ,
        namedrockunit:DRB ,
        namedrockunit:HBB ,
        namedrockunit:SSTV ;
    skos:notation "SUTH"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Sutherland Group"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:SWK
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/J> ;
    lexicon:hasLateralEquivalent
        namedrockunit:LET ,
        namedrockunit:WROT ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/COAL"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/FESTN"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEATM"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Grey mudstone, yellow-grey siltstone and yellow, fine- to coarse-grained sandstone (fluvial, fluvio-deltaic and paralic lithofacies). Sandstones commonly display sharply erosional bases, and channel-fill bedforms. Locally, thin coal seams, seatearth mudstone and nodular sideritic ironstone beds may be present. Plant remains and plant rootlets are common in some beds."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary is taken at the unconformable or disconformable boundary between the underlying heterolithic, marine Dogger Formation (ferruginous sandstone; ironstone; limestone; or calcareous mudstone) and the sandstone, siltstone or mudstone (with plant fragments) of the Saltwick Formation. Where the Dogger Formation is absent due to penecontemporaneous erosion, the Saltwick Formation rests unconformably on grey, calcareous mudstone or siltstone (commonly shelly) of the marine Lias Group, generally the Whitby Mudstone Formation, or on lower stratigraphical units, such as the Redcar Mudstone Formation, near the Market Weighton High."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1213 ,
        namedrockunit:H4356 ,
        namedrockunit:H5069 ,
        namedrockunit:LET ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JA> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.747e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JA> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "About 50m on the North Yorkshire Coast, between Whitby and Scarborough, and inland in the North Yorks Moors and Cleveland Hills; 20 to 25m in the Hambleton Hills on the western escarpment (Powell, et al., 1992; Frost, 1998), thinning southwards to about 5 to 10m in the Howardian Hills."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The upper boundary is taken at the conformable, abrupt upward transition from the plant debris-rich, cross-stratified sandstones, siltstones and mudstones of the Saltwick Formation to the calcareous mudstone, ooidal ironstone or ferruginous sandstone, commonly with shelly fossils, at the base of the Eller Beck Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JA> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 1.709e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Hayburn Beds [Obsolete: use SWK]"@en ,
        "Hayburn Formation [Obsolete: use SWK]"@en ,
        "Lower Deltaic Series [Obsolete: use SWK]"@en ,
        "Lower Estuarine \"Series\" [Obsolete: use CLH, GRF, SWK, EBB, SYCM]"@en ,
        "Wroot Formation"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:RAG ;
    skos:definition "Mudstone, sandstone and siltstone and trace coal, nodular ironstone and seat-earth mudstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Aalenian Age (Jurassic Period) (174.7-170.9 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:notation "SWK"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Saltwick Formation"@en ;
.

namedrockunit:SXCAT
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/C"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CZ"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/P"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/S"^^xsd:anyURI ,
