        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Coarse-grained purple sandstones and grits with subordinate purple mudstones, siltstones and at least three beds of conglomerate."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "At the base of the Bayston - Oakswood Formation massive coarse purplish sandstone with small scattered pebbles rests unconformably upon purple and green shales and sandstones of the Portway Formation. The basal sanstone may reprent the dying out of the Haughmond Conglomerate, which forms the basal member of the Formation, overlying beds that might be equivalent to the Synalds Formation, in the Shrewsbury area."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1327 ,
        namedrockunit:YWO ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AD> ;
