        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/TUF"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Thin- to medium-bedded poorly fossiliferous, calcite mudstones, dolomite mudstones and mudstones. A unit of crinoidal and oolitic limestones occurs in the middle of the Formation, and a 15m-thick unit of oolitic and crinoidal limestone occurs in the upper part of Formation [said to correlate with the Goblin Combe Oolite Formation of Broadfield Down, but this is not proven].  Basalt, tuff and ashy limestone are present in the middle of the Formation on Broadfield Down. Carbonates of the Formation were deposited mainly in a back barrier setting."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at irregular erosive contact of dolomite and calcite mudstones and mudstones of the formation above the clay palaesol of the underlying Gully Oolite Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H118 ,
        namedrockunit:H2066 ,
        namedrockunit:H2067 ,
        namedrockunit:H760 ,
        namedrockunit:LCDM ,
        namedrockunit:UCDM ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.445e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "60 m at Bristol and northern Broadfield Down thinning to a feather edge on the southern side of Broadfield Down."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "In the Bristol area the upper boundary is taken at the sharp contact between the interbedded dolomite and calcite mudstones and mudstones of the formation and the basal sandy limestone of the overlying Clifton Down Limestone Formation. The boundary needs further investigation. In Broadfield Down the upper boundary is taken at the incoming of ooidal limestones of the Goblin Combe Oolite Formation above the interbedded dolomite and calcite mudstones and mudstones of the Clifton Down Mudstone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CJ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.43e+02 ;
