    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A pink, medium-grained muscovite granite, aphyric and porphyritic microgranite, coarse-grained granite, medium-grained granodiorite, microgranodiorite, biotite-rich granodiorite, and quartz-mica greisen locally containing topaz and quartz-andalusite rock associated with granite. The age of the granite is 450 +/- 3 Ma (U-Pb, zircon) (Hughes et al., 1996)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Two sheet-like masses of granite and granodiorite cropping out over 53 and 23 sq. km respectively, and intruded into the Skiddaw Group and the Borrowale Volcanic Group."@en ;
