    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Metagreywacke: interbedded psammite and semipelite with subsidiary pelite. Contains major units of pebbly psammite, particularly in basal part (Knock Head Grit Member). Metamorphosed to slates, phyllites and mica-schists. Contains Boulder Bed at Macduff (glaciomarine diamicton). Minor calc-silicate pods. Contains andalusite, cordierite and locally staurolite porphyroblasts."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Change from calcareous semipelite to non-calcareous lithologies at top of Whitehills Grit Formation; commonly marked by change to locally coarsely gritty psammite of Knock Head Grit Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:DCBD ,
        namedrockunit:DCMS ,
        namedrockunit:H1685 ,
        namedrockunit:H203 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
