    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The term Shetland Group was introduced by Deegan and Scull (1977) for a unit of mudstone with relatively minor interbedded argillaceous limestones lying between the Cromer Knoll and Montrose groups in the Northern North Sea."@en ;
