    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 30 m, and typically 20 m thick in the type area."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Generally a sharp, erosive boundary, with a cross-bedded shell-fragmental ooidal limestone of the Forest Marble Formation or mudstone of the Forest Marble Formation or Blisworth Clay Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/JN> ;
