    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Diamicton, gravel, sand, silt and clay, typically yellowish or greyish brown and containing clasts derived from the Lake District, Shap Fell and the Howgill Fells, including welded tuff (Borrowdale Volcanic Group), slate, granite, granophyre, limestone and sandstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally unconformable on bedrock, but locally unconformable on older deposits of diamicton, gravel, sand, silt and clay assigned to the Central Cumbria (Albion) Glacigenic Subgroup."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:CCDR ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
