        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Reddish brown sands and sandstones, cross-bedded, with intercalated thin lenses and beds of breccia and mudstone. North of Broadclyst, two mappable units predominantly of mudstone have been named: Poltimore Mudstone and Bussell's Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "South of Exminster, interdigitational with Heavitree Breccia. From Exminster to Monkerton (SX 970 940), sharp base on Heavitree Breccia or Monkerton Formation. North of Monkerton to near Broadclyst, rests unconformably on Crackington Formation. In Crediton Trough, rests on Shute Sandstone."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:CLYS ,
        namedrockunit:H1475 ,
        namedrockunit:H188 ,
        namedrockunit:H2739 ,
        namedrockunit:H838 ,
        namedrockunit:H839 ;
