    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Variable across the area and at single locations, but dominated by dark and pale grey, purplish or black crinoidal and coralline limestone, with local staty intercalations of limited lateral extent. Some red shaly compact limestone. Locally, around Yealmpton, dolomite is present, both as massive beds and as intercalated layers with non-dolomitised limestone. Around Buckfastleigh, thick-bedded grey limestones are exposed in several quarries."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Thrust contacts which bring the limestones in to faulted contact with many other rock units."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/DM> ;
