    skos:definition "Mudstone and slaty mudstone with subsidiary basaltic lava, basaltic volcaniclastic-breccia, basaltic-rock, breccia, conglomerate, felsic lava, felsic tuff, granophyric granite, mafic lava, mafic tuff, metabasaltic-rock, pillowed basalt lava, quartzite, rhyolitic pyroclastic-rock, sandstone, schist, trachytic lava and trachytic tuff and trace limestone and ultramafic-rock. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Givetian Age - to - Frasnian Age (Devonian Period) (385.3-371.1 Ma BP)."@en ;
