        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The term Windermere Supergroup was introduced by Kneller et al. (1994) for the folded and cleaved marine carbonate and clastic sedimentary rocks that lie above the unconformity at the top of the Caradoc volcanic rocks in the Lake District and adjacent inliers in northern England, but below unconformably overlying Devonian Old Red Sandstone or basal Carboniferous rocks. The oldest strata, assigned to the Dent Group, are Late Ordovician in age, whilst the remainder are Silurian."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The unconformity at the top of the Caradoc volcanic rocks in the Lake District and adjacent inliers in northern England."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:H2491 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/OLA> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 4.582e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/SG> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "c. 4500 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Unconformably overlain by Devonian Old Red Sandstone or basal Carboniferous rocks."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SO> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 4.19e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel "Windermere Group [Obsolete: use TNTH, WIN]"@en ;
    skos:definition "Siltstone and silty mudstone with subsidiary mudstone and sandstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Late Ordovician Epoch (Ordovician Period) - to - Pridoli Epoch (Silurian Period) (458.2-419 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:isTopConceptOf lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:narrower
        namedrockunit:BBCW ,
        namedrockunit:CTG ,
        namedrockunit:DALBY ,
