    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Grey, weathering yellow or brown, micaceous silt, very fine-grained sand and fine-grained sand, locally with calcite-cemented sandstone beds and lenses, variably sandy clay/mudstone at base, including Downcliff Clay (Member) of type area."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Base of sand/silt or mudstone, as described in the Lithological Description, resting non-sequentially on limestone of the Beacon Limestone Formation or, north of Chipping Sodbury area in the Worcester Basin, a gradational boundary with mudstone of the Whitby Mudstone Formation (q.v.)."@en ;
