    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "From 490-640 m thick according to Carroll (1995), and 730 m thick estimated by Armstrong and Paterson (1970)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The top of the highest bed of laminated, grey siltstone of the Cowie Harbour Siltstone Member, that is conformably overlain by red, cross-bedded, fine- to medium-grained sandstone of the Carron Sandstone Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/SG> ;
