    skos:definition "Diamicton, gravel and sand with subsidiary clay and silt. Stratified superficial deposits. Occurs onshore. Formed during the Early Pleistocene - to - Mid Pleistocene (Quaternary Period) (2.58-.126 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:narrower namedrockunit:BDW ;
