    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A mixed succession of predominantly bedded volcaniclastic rocks, comprising detritus mainly of andesitic composition with bedded volcaniclastic sandstone as the main lithofacies, and subsidiary  units of volcaniclastic breccia, tuff and lapilli-tuff, of which significant units of volcaniclastic breccia and pyroclastic rocks are given member status, the whole intruded by many contemporaneous andesite sills."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Taken at the abrupt change from silicic tuff and lapilli-tuff of the Whelter Knotts Formation, to generally well bedded volcaniclastic rocks."@en ;
