namedrockunit:CNAL
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/AGG"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/BA"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CONG"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Basalt lavas with interbedded agglomerate, conglomerate and sandstone. \r
\r
The Basal Member (CNAL1) occurs on Sanday. \r
\r
On Canna, the Tighard Member (CNAL2), Cnoc Bhrostan Member (CNAL3), Carn a'Ghaill Member (CNAL4), Beul Lama Sgorr Member (CNAL5), and Eilean a'Bhàird Member (CNAL6) are recognised. \r
\r
In north-west Rum the Canna Lava Formation consists of four distinct members: the Lower Fionchra Member (LFION), Upper Fionchra Member (UFION), Guirdil Member (GUIRD), and Orval Member (ORVAL)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GP> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 6.6e+01 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GP> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "On Canna and Sanday, the succession of lavas and fluviatile deposits is over 200 m thick. It is difficult to establish an accurate thickness since faults divide the succession into a number of blocks and individual flows, groups of flows and the conglomerates show abrupt variations in thickness and continuity. The flows dip at low angles (< 3°)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/GP> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 5.6e+01 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:definition "Basalt with subsidiary agglomerate, conglomerate and sandstone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Paleocene Epoch (Palaeogene Period) (66-56 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:isTopConceptOf lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
    skos:narrower
        namedrockunit:CNAL1 ,
        namedrockunit:CNAL2 ,
        namedrockunit:CNAL3 ,
        namedrockunit:CNAL4 ,
        namedrockunit:CNAL5 ,
        namedrockunit:CNAL6 ,
        namedrockunit:GUIRD ,
        namedrockunit:LFION ,
        namedrockunit:ORVAL ,
        namedrockunit:UFION ;
    skos:notation "CNAL"@en ;
    skos:prefLabel "Canna Lava Formation"@en ;
