    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1.653e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "At the composite type section at Brora, the aggregated thickness of the exposed, lower part of the formation is at least 102 m, with an estimated additional 400 m of unexposed strata above."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Change up (not exposed) from sandstone to matrix-supported conglomerate of cobbles and boulders of sandstone, interbedded with laminated siltstone and sandstone (Kintradwell Boulder Beds Member of the Helmsdale Boulder Beds Formation, and Allt Na Cuile Sandstone [Formation])(Wright and Cox, 2001, fig.5.2)."@en ;
