    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Glacial deposits are divided into two classes, proglacial and glacigenic deposits. Proglacial deposits include all sediments deposited by meltwaters in the proglacial environment. Glacigenic deposits are sediments laid down within or under glacier ice or deposited by an ice sheet. \r
\r
Variable lithology."""@en ;
