        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Green-grey, lithic arenites ('Pennant sandstones') with conglomerate lenses at bases of units; thin mudstone/siltstone and seatearth interbeds and mainly thin coals. \r
\r
Age Asturian."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base is placed at the base of the Brithdir Coal, above 'Pennant' sandstones and thin mudstones/siltstones of the Rhondda Member or above red/green mudstones of the Deri Formation on the east crop of the coalfield."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
