    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Limestones, dominated by low-energy calcilutite, and peloidal wackestone and packstone. Commonly includes sandy limestone or calcareous sandstone in basal part (locally known as Collyweston Slate) and contains substantial units of mudstone, particularly from the Lincoln area northwards."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Quasi-conformable or more or less disconformable contact with sandstones and mudstones of the underlying Grantham Formation or, where the latter is absent (mainly in the north), ferruginous sandstone of the Northampton Sand Formation, or mudstone of Lias Group, overlain by limestone or sandy limestone of the Lower Lincolnshire Limestone Member."@en ;
