        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The formation comprises a widespread sheet of well sorted, fine- to medium-grained micaceous, glauconitic, locally shelly sands (Chillesford Sand Member in southeast Suffolk), with localized beds of laminated silty clays (Chillesford Clay and Easton Bavents Clay members) and rounded flint gravels (Westleton Beds). The formation is marine, with the clay members being estuarine and the Westleton Beds representing beach-face gravels."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Rests with discontinuity on the Red Crag Formation and oversteps onto Coralline Crag Formation, Palaeogene formations and Chalk Group bedrock."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1081 ,
        namedrockunit:H1721 ,
