    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Sandstones, mudstones, siltstones and limestones of the Valhall Formation, Rødby Formation, Carrack Formation, Britannia Sandstone Formation and Wick Formation. Originally erected by Rhys (1974), emended by Deegan and Scull (1977) and further revised by Johnson and Lott (1993)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "A downward change from the Valhall and Wick Sandstone formations in the lower part of Cromer Knoll Group to the mainly argillaceous Kimmeridge Clay Formation of the Humber Group."@en ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/KR> ;
