    skos:definition "Gneiss, gneissose granite and gneissose semipelite and trace amphibolite, biotite pegmatite, breccia, calcsilicate-rock, cataclasite, felsic orthogneiss, foliated granite, gneissose metagranodiorite, gneissose metamafic-rock, gneissose pelite, gneissose psammite, granite, granofels, graphitic pelite, hornblende schist, hornblende-bearing orthogneiss, hornblendite, hypersthene metagranodiorite, mafic orthogneiss, magnetitite, marble, melagabbro, meta-anorthosite, meta-ultramafitite, metacarbonate-rock, metalimestone, metamafic-rock, metaperidotite, metasedimentary rock based on grain size or crystal size, metatonalite, metavolcaniclastic-igneous-rock [obsolete code: use +#^ssr], mica schist, mylonite, nebulose granitic-rock, ortho-amphibolite, orthogneiss, pegmatite, pegmatitic granite, pelite, peridotite, protomylonitic gneiss, psammite, pyroxene granofels, pyroxene-bearing gneiss, quartzite, schist, schistose amphibolite, serpentinite and ultramafic-rock. Bedrock. Occurs both onshore and offshore. Formed during the Archean Eon - to - Proterozoic Eon (Precambrian) (4000-541 Ma BP)."@en ;
