    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "c. 80 m"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Between Brushford and Ashbrittle the upper boundary is taken at the incoming of dark grey predominantly unfossiliferous finely laminated silty mudstones with scattered siltstones of the overlying Dowhills Mudstone Formation above the highest limestone bed of the Bampton Limestone Formation."@en ;
