    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Grey, soft, marly, flint-free chalk, typically weathering buff in exposures; locally includes pinkish bands; some harder, gritty, shell-debris-rich beds, and thin discrete marl seams."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The lower boundary is placed at an erosion surface, locally developed on a hardground, overlain by nodular chalk (lowest Cenomanian) of the Paradoxica (or Sponge) Bed or, in the Cleveland Basin, the flaser-bedded white chalks with red or purple marls of the Crowe's Shoot Member (Gaunt et al., 1992; Mitchell, 1995)."@en ;
