    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "A pale to dark grey, crinoidal, and shelly bioclastic limestone, interpreted to be of marine origin, containing argillaceous partings where it is thickly developed."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally seen as a conformable change from marine mudstone overlying the Hurlet Coal at the top of the Lawmuir Formation or West Lothian Oil-Shale Formation in West Lothian, or a coal at the top of the Pathhead Formation in Fife, or Aberlady Formation in East Lothian."@en ;
