    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/B> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "From 0.75m to 1.5m, and locally 11m, in the Airdrie, Falkirk and Glasgow districts. In shelf settings, such as in Midlothian, it can be as much as 14m thick."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Generally seen as a conformable change to thick marine mudstone that passes up into deltaic arenaceous deposits of the Lower Limestone Formation."@en ;
