    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Till is unsorted and unstratified drift, generally overconsolidated, deposited directly by and underneath a glacier without subsequent reworking by water from the glacier. It consists of a heterogenous mixture of clay, sand, gravel, and boulders varying widely in size and shape (diamicton). Synonym: boulder clay. Obsolete: pinnel."@en ;
