    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "The formation includes a complex, commonly thinly interbedded sequence of sands, gravels, silt clays, pebbly clay diamictons and stony sandy clay diamictons (tills) containing clasts from Scotland and the northern Irish Sea basin and the west Cumbrian coalfield, as well as from the western Lake District."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally undulating erosional contact on to older sequences including the Ravenglass Till Member of the Seascale Glacigenic Formation."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H1570 ,
        namedrockunit:H4662 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/QD> ;
