namedrockunit:FELL
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/COAL"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LMST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/PESST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEATS"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SLST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Onshore areas: \r
\r
Medium- to thick-bedded, fine- to coarse-grained cross-bedded sandstone, locally conglomeratic, with siltstone, mudstone, seatearth and locally developed thin coals and limestones. \r
\r
Offshore areas: \r
\r
The Fell Sandstone Formation is characterized by massive, pale grey and white, fine to medium or coarse grained, poorly sorted sandstones. However, it also contains sporadic beds of grey, blocky to subfissile, non-calcareous mudstone that are up to 10 m thick, and occasional beds of dark grey, pyritic, carbonaceous mudstone. In well 43/2-1, the sandstones are partly cemented by silica. \r
\r
In well 44/2-1, a basal 80 m-thick sandstone unit includes partings of argillaceous dolomite, and is overlain by 12 m of thinly bedded shales and dolomites. Middle and upper massive sandstone units, 106 m and 98 m thick respectively, are separated by a 40 m-thick, relatively argillaceous interval that includes yellowish brown, reddish brown and grey mudstones."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition """Onshore areas: \r
\r
Locally unconformable, diachronous base on range of Lower Carboniferous strata, locally defined as base of Whitberry Marine Bed. \r
\r
Offshore areas: \r
\r
An erosion surface separates the Fell Sandstone and Cementstone groups at the Berwickshire coast (Smith, 1967). The base of the Fell Sandstone Formation in well 43/2-1 is defined by a downward change from massive sandstones to interbedded mudstones, sandstones and limestones. It is marked by a sharp downward increase in gamma values. In well 44/2-1, the Fell Sandstone rests on thinly interbedded cementstones and clastic sediments; the boundary is taken at the top of the highest cementstone bed, and is marked by a high-velocity spike. Smith's observation (1967) that, uniquely within the lower Dinantian, the onshore Fell sandstones lack mica, argillaceous and carbonaceous detritus, may prove useful in locating the boundary in gradational offshore sections."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:CSG ,
        namedrockunit:FLS ,
        namedrockunit:MBG ,
        namedrockunit:MBO ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CI> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.467e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/F> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription """Onshore areas: \r
\r
c. 530 m maximum. \r
\r
Offshore areas: \r
\r
382 m thick in well 43/2-1 and 338 m thick in well 44/2-1."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition """Onshore areas: \r
\r
Locally unconformable, diachronous, at base of Clattering Marine Bed, Kingsbridge Limestone or Glencartholm Volcanic Member of the Tyne Limestone Formation. \r
\r
Offshore areas: \r
\r
In the two offshore wells that have penetrated the Fell Sandstone / Scremerston formational boundary, it is defined by an abrupt facies transition from massive sandstones to argillaceous coal measures. This transition is marked by a sharp downhole decrease in gamma-ray response in well 43/2-1. A thin coal seam occurs close above the facies transition in well 44/2-1."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CQ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.37e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel
        "Border Group, Middle [Obsolete: use FELL]"@en ,
        "Craighill Sandstone Group [Obsolete: use FELL]"@en ,
        "Fell Sandstone Group [Obsolete: use FELL]"@en ,
        "Middle Border Group [Obsolete: use FELL]"@en ;
