\r
Bolsovian to Asturian."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base of the Member is placed at the base of the No.2 Rhondda Coal in the type area of the Rhondda valleys; the seam is named the Llwydcoed Seam in the Ammanford district and the Wernddu in the Swansea district. The coal rests conformably on lithic ('Pennant') sandstones and thin mudstones/siltstones of the underlying Llynfi Member."@en ;
