namedrockunit:CLWYD
    a skos:Concept ;
    lexicon:hasBroaderPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/C> ;
    lexicon:hasLateralEquivalent namedrockunit:DINA ;
    lexicon:hasLithology
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/CHRT"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/DOLMST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/LMST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/MDST"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SDST"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """The Visean succession of North Wales comprises a sequence of dominantly shallow marine ramp and platform carbonates defined as the Clwyd Limestone Group. \r
\r
The succession comprises the Foel Formation, overlain by the Llanarmon Limestone Formation. This is overlain by the Leete Limestone Formation and in turn by the Loggerheads Limestone Formation. The upper part of the group comprises the Cefn Mawr Limestone Formation. This is locally overlain by the Red Wharf Limestone Formation or Minera Formation. \r
\r
A diverse range of limestone facies with subordinate sandstone and mudstone units, and exhibiting local dolomitisation. \r
\r
Visean 'knoll reef' limestones are recognised in the Llandudno and Prestatyn areas (Warren et al., 1984) and channelised sandstone and conglomerate bodies are a feature of the succession exposed on Anglesey (Davies, J R, 1991). \r
\r
The group records the initiation and growth of a carbonate platform along the northern flank of the Wales-Brabant Massif."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The group rests locally upon several formations formerly collectively known as 'Basement Beds', or elsewhere with marked unconformity on Silurian rocks."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:DYL ,
        namedrockunit:GRN ,
        namedrockunit:H2100 ,
        namedrockunit:H2703 ,
        namedrockunit:H4550 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CV> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 3.467e+02 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CV> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/G> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "The group is up to 900 m thick."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Conformable base of Pentre Chert Formation or Cefn-y-fedw Sandstone Formation in northeast Wales. Elsewhere marked by an unconformity with younger Carboniferous or Permo-Triassic rocks."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CV> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 3.303e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
