        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/QZITE"^^xsd:anyURI ,
        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/SEMPEL"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription "Diamictite ('Boulder Bed') with limestone clasts in its lower part and quartzite and granite clasts in upper part attains maximum thickness in Port Askaig area and on Garvellachs; overlying quartzite reaches 5km in thickness on Jura but is more usually 0.5 - 1km thick; dolomitic beds are locally developed near base of quartzite. In Ladder Hills area graded psammites and semipelites intervene between diamictite and quartzite."@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Generally transitional over a few metres at base of tillite of Port Askaig (Schiehallion) Boulder Bed."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent namedrockunit:DBBT ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAgeValue 1e+03 ;
    lexicon:hasPredominantAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasRockUnitRank <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Lexicon/RockUnitRank/UG> ;
    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "Up to 5km"@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "Abrupt transition from quartzite to graphitic pelite (Easdale) or mixed psammite, semipelite and pelite (Perthshire)."@en ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/AZ> ;
    lexicon:hasYoungestAgeValue 5.41e+02 ;
    dcterms:source "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/ref/Lexicon/NamedRockUnit"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    reg:status <https://linked.data.gov.au/def/reg-statuses/stable> ;
    skos:altLabel "Tillite (Banffshire) [Obsolete: use DBIS, DBST, DBPT]"@en ;
    skos:broader namedrockunit:ARGY ;
    skos:definition "Diamictite and quartzite with subsidiary dolomitic limestone, pelite, psammite and semipelite and trace micaceous psammite. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Neoproterozoic Era (Precambrian) (1000-541 Ma BP)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme lexicon:NamedRockUnit ;
