    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Green-grey, lithic arenites ('Pennant sandstones'), with thin mudstone/siltstone and seatearth interbeds, and mainly thin coals. \r
\r
Age Asturian."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "The base is placed at the base of the Hughes Coal or its equivalent (Cefn Glas, Wenallt, Bettws Four-Feet, Ty-du, etc.) in a predominantly arenaceous sequence of the Pennant Sandstone Formation, where the coal rests on mudstone/siltstone seatearth at the top of the Brithdir Member."@en ;
    lexicon:hasObsoleteEquivalent
        namedrockunit:H2226 ,
        namedrockunit:H946 ;
    lexicon:hasOldestAge <http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/Geochronology/Division/CAS> ;
