        "http://data.bgs.ac.uk/id/EarthMaterialClass/RockClassAll/Z"^^xsd:anyURI ;
    lexicon:hasLithologyDescription """Tills (diamictons), sands, gravels, silts and clays. Sands and gravels contain clasts derived from rocks cropping out throughout northern, central and eastern England, Scotland and Wales, and offshore. \r
\r
A suite of glacial, glaciofluvial, glaciolacustrine and glaciomarine deposits. \r
\r
Cromerian - pre-Ipswichian (MIS 16 - 6)."""@en ;
    lexicon:hasLowerBoundaryDefinition "Sharp, planar unconformable contact with units of the Dunwich and/or Crag groups, or bedrock."@en ;
