    skos:definition "Conglomerate, pelite, quartzite and semipelite with subsidiary amphibolite, basalt, psammite and volcaniclastic rocks (both pyroclastic and reworked volcanic rocks) and trace calcsilicate-rock, graphitic pelite and metalimestone. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Neoproterozoic Era (Precambrian) (1000-541 Ma BP)."@en ;
