    lexicon:hasThicknessDescription "The Strathclyde Group exceeds 1250 m in thickness. Paterson and Hall (1986) suggested it is about 1500 m thick in the type area. It may locally exceed 2000 m."@en ;
    lexicon:hasUpperBoundaryDefinition "The base of the Clackmannan Group (mixed shelf carbonate and deltaic ('Yoredale') facies of a variable succession) defines the top of the Strathclyde Group."@en ;
