    skos:definition "Mudstone and sandstone with subsidiary basalt, coal, ironstone, limestone, pebbly (gravelly) sandstone, sapropelite, seat-earth sandstone, siltstone and volcaniclastic-sedimentary-rock and trace basaltic tuff, mugearite, nodular limestone (cornstone), olivine-clinopyroxene-macrophyric basaltic-rock, plagioclase-macrophyric basaltic-rock, plagioclase-olivine-clinopyroxene-macrophyric basalt, plagioclase-olivine-clinopyroxene-macrophyric basaltic-rock, trachybasalt, trachytic-rock and tuff. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Chadian Substage - to - Brigantian Substage (Carboniferous Period) (346.7-330.3 Ma BP)."@en ;
