    skos:definition "Metasedimentary rock based on grain size or crystal size and wacke with subsidiary chert, lava and mudstone and trace gritty psammite, hornblende schist, magnetite-bearing schistose psammite, metalava, metalimestone, metatuff, metawacke, mica schist, micaceous psammite, pelite, psammite, schist and semipelite. Stratified bedrock. Occurs onshore. Deposited during the Neoproterozoic Era (Precambrian) - to - St David's Series (Cambrian Period) (1000-499 Ma BP)."@en ;
